2 CONC antinus in 581 Mauricius had defeated the Persian Great King Hormizdas IV after a four-year-long campaign. He married Constantia, the emperor's daughter, by whom he had eight children. He took over a bankrupt state, something whic
2 CONC h forced him to extreme parsimony, but earned him a reputation for avarice among the people and the mercenaries.
