2 CONT Mardanshah was a 7th-century Sasanian prince. He was the son of the Sasanian shah Khosrau II and Shirin, and was the preferred successor of the Sasanian Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was later killed along with his brothers and half-brothers by his half-brother Kavadh II in 628
