2 CONC terests as a minority religion," observes Patrick Amory, People and Identity in Ostrogothic Italy, 489-554, p. 216.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.^ The incident is reported only in the Anonymous Valesianus (Amory p. 216); "The Anonymous Valesianus covered the period 474—526 essentially from a Catholic-exarchate point of view and was probably written near Ravenna ca 527." 
2 CONC (Thomas S. Burns, The Ostrogoths: kingship and society‎, 1980:66).
