1 NOTE {geni:about_me} His full name was Flavius Iustinus Augustus. He was Emperor of the Eastern Roman Empire (518). He was an old man when he became Emperor, and is said to have been completely illiterate (unheard of for a Roman). Even
2 CONC  though Justinian, his nephew, was still young, he was the one who ran the Eastern Empire during Justin's reign. Justin was succeeded by Justinian as Emperor on his death in 527.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Occupation: Emperor of Byzantium 
