1 NOTE Theodorico é citado pela wikipédia mas não há menção a sua filha Theodora. Sobre seus filhos e esposas, é dito: 
2 CONT Theodoric was married once.
2 CONT He had a concubine in Moesia, name unknown, and had two daughters:
2 CONT     * Theodegotha (ca. 473 – ?). In 494, she was married to Alaric II as a part of her father's alliance with the Visigoths.
2 CONT     * Ostrogotha or Arevagni (ca. 475 – ?). In 494 or 496, she was married to the king Sigismund of Burgundy as a part of her father's alliance with the Burgundians.
2 CONT Married to Audofleda in 493 and had one daughter:
2 CONT     * Amalasuntha, Queen of the Goths. She was married to Eutharic and had two children: Athalaric and Matasuentha (the latter being married to Witiges first, then, after Witiges' death, married to Germanus Justinus, neither had c
2 CONC hildren). Any hope for a reconciliation between the Goths and the Romans in the person of a Gotho-Roman Emperor from this family lineage was shattered.
1 NOTE Theodoric the Great, King of the Ostrogoths
2 CONT Born: c454
