2 CONT Amalasuntha
2 CONT
2 CONT King of the Ostrogoths 474-526
2 CONT From ages 7 to 17 he was a Byzantine prisoner, but returned to hisfather's kingdom after and became king in 474 at the death of his father.Between 474 and 488, Theodoric and the Eastern Roman Emperor Zeno foughteach other. In 488 
2 CONC Theodoric, while allied with Zeno, invaded Italy (atthe time under the Germanic king Odoacer), which was taken in threebattles. Odoacer surrendered in 493, and was slain by Theodoric. WhileTheodoric was Arian, he tolerated all sec
2 CONC ts of Christianity. Theodoricwas succeeded on this death in 526 by his daughter Amalasuntha as regentfor her son Athalaric.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.ghg.net/shetler/oldimp/017.html
