1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogical Chart
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.entrybytroops.org/bahaullahs-genealogy.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://akevoth.org/genealogy/duparc/3702.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Izdundar's husband, Bustanai (d. 660/5) was the first Jewish Exilarch to be recognized by Arab rule. His birth and much of his life is surrounded by legend. Izdundwar, the daughter of the King of Persia, was Bustanai's second wife
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife, Adoa, a Davidic Jewish princess (relative), had two sons: Hisdai I & Baradai; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father, Yazdgerd III (also spelled Yazdegerd or Yazdiger, Persian: یزدگرد سوم, "made by God"), was the twenty-ninth and last king of the Sassanid dynasty of Iran and a grandson of Khosrau II (590–628). 
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was Shahryar whose mother was Miriam, the daughter of the Byzantine Emperor Maurice. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Bahai religious leader Bahá'u'lláh's ancestry can be traced back to Yazdgerd III.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://akevoth.org/genealogy/duparc/3702.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.american-pictures.com/genealogy/persons/per03115.htm#0
2 CONT
2 CONT Bustani 2nd wife, Dara or Azdadwar Izdundad or Izdadwar daughter of Zamaspdukht and King Yazdeger /Shahrijar III of Persia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Persian princess given by Omar/Caliph Ali (?) as a slave to Bustenai. He proceeded to free her and to marry her after she converted to Judaism
2 CONT
2 CONT The Parthi princess, had three sons: (a) Hisdai II , (b) Nehemiah , and (c) Haninai [Hananiah], who was "exilarch" of Sura 689-694.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://akevoth.org/genealogy/duparc/3702.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Bustanai (d. 660/5) was the first Exilarch to be recognized by Arab rule.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a token of appreciation, Caliph Ali gave him the daughter of the Persian king Yazdeger (Yazadagird III of Parthia ) for a slave. Eventually Bustanai married her, as his 2nd wife, 
2 CONT
2 CONT She gave birth to three sons: (a) Hisdai II , (b) Nehemiah , and (c) Haninai [Hananiah], who was "exilarch" of Sura 689-694.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Izdudad was also called Dara, and also Izdadwar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Izdundad, Princess of Iran, married Exilarch Bustanai ben Haninai beni David, son of Exilarch Haninai I ben Hofnai beni David in 657.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p106.htm#i12951 )
2 CONT
2 CONT from Compiler: R. B. Stewart, Evans, GA
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/index.htm )
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT According to one account, the Caliph Omar (father-in-law of Muhammad) confirmed Bustanai as Exilarch of the Jews after the Arabian conquest of Persia, and gave Bustanai the daughter of Chosroes II as his wife, while Omar married h
2 CONC er sister. But according to another account, given in Abraham ibn Daud's, Seder ha-Kabbalah (12th century), the Caliph was Muhammad's son-in-law Ali and the father of Bustanai's Persian wife was Yezdagird III.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Justin Swanstrom, 12/31/2010
