2 CONT >1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Child%C3%A9ric-I-King-of-the-Franks/6000000005913253971?through=6000000005913350166 CHILDERICH] (-Tournai [481/82], bur Tournai). 
2 CONT > m ([464]) as her second husband, [https://www.geni.com/people/Basina-II-of-the-Th%C3%BCringians/6000000003772264436?through=6000000005913350166 BASINA], formerly wife of BASINUS King of Thuringia, daughter of -.  King Childerich
2 CONC  & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>a)        ''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Clovis-I-the-Great-King-of-the-Franks/6000000005913350166?through=6000000005913253971 CHLODOVECH] [Clovis] ([464/67]-Paris [27 Nov] 511, bur Paris, basilique des Saints-Apôtres [later é
2 CONC glise de Sainte-Geneviève]).  Gregory of Tours names Clovis as son of Childerich & Basina[26].  He succeeded his father in [481/82] as CLOVIS I King of the Franks. CHLODOVECH [Clovis], son of CHILDERICH I King of the Franks & his 
2 CONC wife Basina --- ([464/67]-Paris [27 Nov] 511, bur Paris, basilique des Saints-Apôtres [later église de Sainte-Geneviève]).  Gregory of Tours names Clovis as son of Childerich & Basina[37].  The Liber Historiæ Francorum names "Chil
2 CONC derico" as father of "Chlodovecho rege"[38].  He succeeded his father in [481/82] as CLOVIS I King of the Franks.  He defeated Syagrius, ruler at Soissons, in 486.  The Liber Historiæ Francorum records that "Chlodovechus" expanded
2 CONC  his kingdom "usque Sequanam" and afterwards "usque Ligere fluvio"[39].  He remained a pagan after his marriage to a Catholic wife, but converted to Christianity in [496] allegedly having vowed to do so if successful in a battle a
2 CONC gainst the Alamans[40].  He allied with Godegisel against Gondebaud King of Burgundy in [500][41].  He defeated and killed Alaric II King of the Visigoths at the campus Vogladensis[42], probably Voulan, near Poitiers, athough this
2 CONC  is popularly known as the battle of Vouillé[43], in 507.  Gregory of Tours records that Clovis took control of the territory of Sigebert King of the Franks of the Rhine, after persuading Sigeric's son Chloderic to kill his father
2 CONC  and then killing Chloderic, as well as the territory of Chararic King of the Salian Franks[44].  Gregory of Tours records the death of King Clovis in Paris "five years after the battle of Vouillé" and his burial in the church of 
2 CONC the Holy Apostles, which he and Queen Clotilde had built[45]. Gregory of Tours records that Queen Clotilde became a nun at the church of St Martin at Tours after her husband died, and in a later passage records her death in Tours 
2 CONC and burial in Paris next to her husband in the church which she had built[53].  She was canonised by the Catholic church, feast day 3 Jun[54]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisIB MEDLANDS]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>[m firstly] ---, daughter of --- [of the Franks of the Rhine].  According to Gregory of Tours, the mother of Theoderich was one of King Clovis's concubines not his first wife[46].  Settipani[47] suggests that Theoderich’s mother
2 CONC  was a Frank from the Rhine region, based on the inheritance of Austrasia by Theoderich and the roots "Theode-" and "-rich" in his name, possibly transmitted through his mother from Theodemer and Richomer who were both 4th century
2 CONC  Frankish kings. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisIB MEDLANDS] King Clovis & his first [wife/concubine] had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Th%C3%A9odoric-I-King-of-Austrasia/6000000011570561698?through=6000000005913350166 THEODERICH] ([485]-end 533, bur Metz).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>m [secondly] (492) [https://www.geni.com/people/Chlotilde-of-Burgundy/6000000001947211337 CHROTECHILDIS] [Clotilde/Rotilde[48]] of Burgundy, daughter of CHILPERICH King of Burgundy & his wife --- ([480]-Tours, monastery of Saint
2 CONC -Martin 544 or 548, bur Paris, basilique des Saints-Apôtres [later église de Sainte-Geneviève]).  Gregory of Tours names "Clotilde" as the younger daughter of Chilperich, recording that she and her sister were driven into exile by
2 CONC  their paternal uncle King Gundobad, but that the latter accepted a request for her hand in marriage from Clovis King of the Franks[49].  Fredegar states that she was driven into exile to Geneva by her uncle, after he allegedly mu
2 CONC rdered her father, and that King Clovis requested her hand in marriage as a means of controlling Gundobad's power[50].  A charter dated 2 Oct [499], classified as spurious in the collection, of "Clodoveus rex Francorum" names "uxo
2 CONC ris meæ Chrochildis…patris Chilperici regis Burgundiorum"[51].  Gregory of Tours records Clotilde's lack of success in converting her husband to Christianity until the fifteenth year of his reign, when he and his people were bapti
2 CONC sed by St Rémy Bishop of Reims[52].  Gregory of Tours records that Queen Clotilde became a nun at the church of St Martin at Tours after her husband died, and in a later passage records her death in Tours and burial in Paris next 
2 CONC to her husband in the church which she had built[53].  She was canonised by the Catholic church, feast day 3 Jun[54]. King Clovis & his second wife had [six] children:[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisIB MEDL
2 CONC ANDS] & http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BURGUNDY%20KINGS.htm#ChrotechildisOrClotildedied544
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>2.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Ingomer/6000000003098272663?through=6000000005913350166 INGOMER] (b and d 493). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>3.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Chlodomir-I-King-the-Franks-at-Orl%C3%A9ans/6000000010395927288?through=6000000005913350166 CHLODOMER] ([494/95]-killed in battle Vézeronce 21 Jun 524).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>4.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Child%C3%A9bert-I-King-of-the-Franks-at-Paris/6000000007815238292?through=6000000005913350166 CHILDEBERT] ([497]-23 Dec 558, bur Paris, Saint-Germain des Prés). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>5.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Chlothar-I-the-Old-King-of-the-Franks/5585928797380086234?through=6000000005913350166 CHLOTHACHAR] [Clotaire/Lothar] ([501/02]-Soissons [30 Nov/31 Dec] 561, bur Soissons, basilique Saint-
2 CONC Médard).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>6.         THEODECHILDIS ([492/501]-576).  A charter dated 2 Oct [499], classified as spurious in the collection, of "Clodoveus rex Francorum" purports to be written when "filia mea…Theodechildis" was becoming a nun[133].  As n
2 CONC oted above, the editor of the Monumenta Germaniæ Scriptores series assumes that this charter refers to the daughter of King Theoderich[134].  Another charter, classified as spurious, in the name of "Theodechildis filia Chlodoveo" 
2 CONC purports to record a donation to the monastery of St Peter at Sens dated Sep 569[135].  She founded the monastery of Mauriac in Auvergne[136].  m ---, king.] 
