2 CONT Mosel, 492 married Catholic Burgundian Clothilde, 498 was baptized Catholic, made war against King of Burgundy Gundebald
2 CONT through an alliance with his brother Gondegisel to go after Gundebald entirely in close to those he had driven his field and his life
2 CONT against a serious estimate anexeerde in all 508 small Frankish kingdoms in Francia and killed most of his relatives to
2 CONT erfopvolgingsproblemen to avoid the same year he received recognition from the emperor Anastasius him apart from many titles as well son
2 CONT adopted it, a submission to Byzantium, the Franks for the start of their freedom, organized a council of Orleans in July 511, the first
2 CONT enkerk time that is united, died shortly afterwards in Paris that he had made capital of his empire
1 NOTE "The [December 25, 496] baptism of Clovis was an event of very great importance.  From that time the orthodox Christians in the kingdom of the Burgundians and Visigoths looked to Clovis to deliver them from their Arian kings. . . 
2 CONC He was the true founder of the Frankish monarchy." - E.B. 11th ed., 6:563-4
