2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Italy Kings (covering Theodomir's wife and children):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ITALY,%20Kings%20to%20962.htm#Theodemirdied474B
2 CONT
2 CONT THEODEMIR [Thiudimir], son of VANDALARIUS (-Kyrrhos 474).
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---. The name of Theodemir's wife is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Concubine: ERELEUVA [Erelieva].
2 CONT
2 CONT She was baptised a Catholic as EUSEBIA[233]. Iordanes names "Erelieva concubina" as mother of Theodoric[234]. She went with her son to Italy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodemir & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. AMALAFRIDA (-murdered [523/25]).
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Amalfridam germanam suam [Theoderici]" as the mother of "Theodehadi" and wife of "Africa regi Vandalorum…Thrasamundo"[235]. Emperor Zeno used her as ambassador to her half-brother in 487 to thwart his attack on Con
2 CONC stantinople[236]. Her second marriage was arranged by her half-brother, Theodoric King of Italy, as part of his efforts to foster the support of the Vandals. Amalafrida's dowry was Lilybæum in western Sicily[237].
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of her husband, she unsuccessfully protested his successor's withdrawal of support from her brother, but she was outmanœuvred and killed[238].
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly [HUGO ---] (-before 500). The Widukindi Res Gestæ Saxonicæ names "Huga rex Francorum…unicam filiam Amalbergam" who married "Irminfredo regi Thuringorum"[239], but there is no indication to whom "Huga rex Francorum" could
2 CONC  refer.
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly ([500]) THRASAMUND, King of the Vandals, son of [GENTO the Vandal or GELIMER the Vandal] (before 460-523). Amalafrida & her first husband had two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodemir had three illegitimate children by his concubine:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. THEODORIC ([451][258]-30 Aug 526).
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Theodericum" as son of Theodemir, in a later passage naming his mother "Erelieva concubina"[259]. He was proclaimed THEODORIC "the Great" King of Italy in Mar 493 after defeating King Odovacar.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. THEODIMUND.
2 CONT
2 CONT The primary source which names him has not yet been identified. He marched westwards to Durazzo with his brother in 479, leading one of the three marching columns[260].
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. daughter (-[479]).
2 CONT
2 CONT The primary source which records her existence has not yet been identified. She died about the time her half-brother marched westwards to Durazzo[261].
2 CONT
