1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''AMALAFRIDA (-murdered [523/25])'''
2 CONT d/o THEODEMIR [Thiudimir] 
2 CONT x [HUGO] (-< 500)
2 CONT *THEODAHAD (-murdered Dec 536) King of Italy x GUDELIVA
2 CONT * AMALABERGA  x c 510 HERMANFRED, King of the Thuringians (-534). 
2 CONT xx c 500 THRASAMUND, King of the Vandals, s/o [GENTO the Vandal or GELIMER the Vandal] (<460-523)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ITALY,%20Kings%20to%20962.htm#Theodemirdied474B
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From English Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amalafrida '''Amalafrida''']  (Gothic: 𐌰𐌼𐌰𐌻𐌰𐍆𐍂𐌹𐌳𐌰; before 475 – fl. 523), was queen of the Vandals by marriage to [https://www.geni.com/people/Thrasamund-king-of-the-Vandals/6000000000712707579?throu
2 CONC gh=6000000003827147352 Thrasamund].  She was the daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodomir-king-of-the-Ostrogoths/6000000000508474079?through=6000000003827147352 Theodemir], king of the Ostrogoths, and his wife [sic: conc
2 CONC ubine] [https://www.geni.com/people/Ereleuva-concubine-of-Theodimir/6000000002236412009?through=6000000000508474079 Erelieva]. She was the sister of [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodoric-the-Great-king-of-the-Ostrogoths/600000000
2 CONC 0495138391?through=6000000002236412009 Theodoric the Great], and mother of [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodahad-King-of-the-Ostrogoths/6000000003380698484?through=6000000003827147352 Theodahad], both of whom also were kings of t
2 CONC he Ostrogoths.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 500, Theodoric, ruler over the Ostrogothic Kingdom in Italy, arranged a marriage alliance with Thrasamund, king of the Vandals in North Africa, to further cement his authority over the Vandals. Thrasamund became Amalfrida's sec
2 CONC ond husband. She brought a very large dowry, but also 1 000 Gothic elite warriors plus 5 000 armed retainers.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT After her husband Thrasamund's death, his successor [https://www.geni.com/people/Hilderic-King-of-the-Vandals-Alans/6000000009987656008 Hilderic] issued orders for the return of all the Catholic bishops from exile, and Boniface, a
2 CONC  strenuous asserter of orthodoxy, bishop of the African Church. In response, Amalfrida headed a party of revolt; she called in the assistance of the Moors, and battle was joined at Capsa, about three hundred miles to the south of 
2 CONC the capital Carthage, on the edge of the Libyan desert.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 523, Amalafrida's party was beaten, and Hilderic had her arrested and imprisoned in a successful bid to overthrow Ostrogothic hegemony; he also had her Gothic soldiers killed. She died in prison, exact date unknown.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Amalafrida had two children, the aforementioned Theodahad and [https://www.geni.com/people/Amalaberga-Queen-of-the-Thuringii/6000000013363268226?through=6000000003827147352 Amalaberga], who married [https://www.geni.com/people/Her
2 CONC manfried-king-of-the-Th%C3%BCringians/6000000013363233248?through=6000000013363268226 Hermanfrid], king of the Thuringii. It is not known who the father of these children was. [sic: thought to be https://www.geni.com/people/Hugo-R
2 CONC ex-Francorum/6000000009304845819?through=6000000003827147352]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ITALY,%20Kings%20to%20962.htm#Amalafrida
2 CONT
2 CONT .         AMALAFRIDA (-murdered [523/25]).  Iordanes names "Amalfridam germanam suam [Theoderici]" as the mother of "Theodehadi" and wife of "Africa regi Vandalorum…Thrasamundo"[237].  Emperor Zeno used her as ambassador to her ha
2 CONC lf-brother in 487 to thwart his attack on Constantinople[238].  Her second marriage was arranged by her half-brother, Theodoric King of Italy, as part of his efforts to foster the support of the Vandals.  Amalafrida's dowry was Li
2 CONC lybæum in western Sicily[239].  After the death of her husband, she unsuccessfully protested his successor's withdrawal of support from her brother, but she was outmanœuvred and killed[240].  m firstly [HUGO ---] (-before 500).  T
2 CONC he Widukindi Res Gestæ Saxonicæ names "Huga rex Francorum…unicam filiam Amalbergam" who married "Irminfredo regi Thuringorum"[241], but there is no indication to whom "Huga rex Francorum" could refer.  m secondly ([500]) THRASAMUN
2 CONC D, King of the Vandals, son of [GENTO the Vandal or GELIMER the Vandal] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Summary
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationships
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT *Father: Theodemir or Thiudimir, Co-King of the Ostrogoths (451-468), King of the Ostrogoths (468-474)
2 CONT *Mother: Unknown wife (not Ereleuva, Theodemir's concubine)
2 CONT
2 CONT Half-Siblings (children of Ereleuva):
2 CONT *1. Theoderic I (b. c451), King of the Ostrogoths (474 - 30 August 526)
2 CONT *2. Theodimund (fl. 479)
2 CONT *3. Unknown daughter (d. c479)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses and children:
2 CONT *First Husband: Hugo Rex Francorum (Peter Heather from the English Wikipedia page apparently does not identify this individual, but FMG does)
2 CONT **1. Theodahad, King of Italy (d. December 536, murdered by his own men mid-flight from battle near Rome toward Ravenna, m. Gudeliva and had two children)
2 CONT **2. Amalaberga, Queen of the Thuringians (510-534, m. Hermanafred, King of the Thuringians, died after 534 in Ravenna)
2 CONT *Second Husband: Thrasamund (b. before 460), King of the Vandals (496-523)
2 CONT
2 CONT Basic information:
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 455/460 according to Mittelalter Genealogie. The Ostrogoths under her father didn't leave Pannonia until 473, so this is likely her birth location.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: Unknown, but Arian Christian
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage:
2 CONT *1. Before 500 - Hugo Rex Francorum
2 CONT *2. 500 - Thrasamund, King of the Vandals
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 525 - imprisoned in Carthago
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: 
2 CONT *Before 500, wife of Hugo Rex Francorum (an unknown Frankish King named Hugo)
2 CONT *500-523, Queen of the Vandals, or wife of King Thrasamund of the Vandals.
2 CONT *523-525, prisoner in Carthago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate Names: Amalafrida, Amalfrida, Amalafréde
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Italy Kings:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ITALY,%20Kings%20to%20962.htm#Amalafrida
2 CONT
2 CONT THEODEMIR [Thiudimir], son of VANDALARIUS (-Kyrrhos 474).  Iordanes names "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir" as the sons of Vandilarius[231].  King of the Ostrogoths in Pannonia, under his brother Valamir, he ruled over the western
2 CONC  part of their domain which covered the county of Somogy and northeastern Croatia.  He succeeded his brother in [468/49] as King of all the Pannonian Ostrogoths.  When the Ostrogoths left Pannonia in [473], Theodemir and his conti
2 CONC ngent went towards Constantinople.  They were settled in Macedonia, based in the city of Kyrrhos[232]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Theodemir's wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Concubine:  ERELEUVA [Erelieva].  She was baptised a Catholic as EUSEBIA[233].  Iordanes names "Erelieva concubina" as mother of Theodoric[234].  She went with her son to Italy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodemir & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. AMALAFRIDA (-murdered [523/25]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Amalfridam germanam suam [Theoderici]" as the mother of "Theodehadi" and wife of "Africa regi Vandalorum…Thrasamundo"[235].  Emperor Zeno used her as ambassador to her half-brother in 487 to thwart his attack on Co
2 CONC nstantinople[236].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Her second marriage was arranged by her half-brother, Theodoric King of Italy, as part of his efforts to foster the support of the Vandals.  Amalafrida's dowry was Lilybæum in western Sicily[237].  
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of her husband, she unsuccessfully protested his successor's withdrawal of support from her brother, but she was outmanœuvred and killed[238].  
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly [HUGO ---] (-before 500).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Widukindi Res Gestæ Saxonicæ names "Huga rex Francorum…unicam filiam Amalbergam" who married "Irminfredo regi Thuringorum"[239], but there is no indication to whom "Huga rex Francorum" could refer.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly ([500]) THRASAMUND, King of the Vandals, son of [GENTO the Vandal or GELIMER the Vandal] (before 460-523).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Amalafrida & her first husband had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a) THEODAHAD (-murdered Dec 536).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Amalfridam germanam suam [Theoderici]" as the mother of "Theodehadi qui postea rex fuit" but does not name his father[240].  Disappointed in not succeeding his uncle King Theodoric, Theodahad acquired considerable 
2 CONC private estates in Tuscany "where he led a retired life at home" according to Jordanes[241].  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was planning to sell this "kingdom" to the emperor, in return for retirement in Constantinople and an annual pension, when his cousin Queen Amalasuintha recalled him and appointed him co-regent in 534[242].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Procopius records that “Theodatus, filius Amalafridas sororis Theoderici” possessed "agrorum Tusciæ" and planned to deliver "Tusciam in Iustiniani Augusti potestatem"[243].  In a later passage, Procopius records that “Theodatus” w
2 CONC as appointed regent by "Amalasuntha"[244].  
2 CONT
2 CONT He arrested the Queen end-534 and imprisoned her on an island in Lake Bolsena[245], assuming the title THEODAHAD King of Italy.  Iordanes records that "Theodahadum consobrinum suum" succeeded Athalric, appointed by the latter's mo
2 CONC ther whom Theodahad killed soon after his accession[246].  
2 CONT
2 CONT After the Queen's murder, Emperor Justinian ordered a two-pronged attack against Sicily and Dalmatia in revenge.  Theodahad repelled the initial threat in Dalmatia in 536, but an imperial fleet occupied Split and Dubrovnik.  The f
2 CONC orces in Sicily, under Belisarius, moved into mainland Italy, occupied Naples.  Theodahad marched as far as Rome to meet the invaders, but was murdered while trying to escape back to Ravenna[247].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m GUDELIVA, daughter of ---.  The primary source which names the wife of Theodahad has not so far been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodahad & his wife had two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT b)   AMALABERGA .  
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Amalabergam" as the daughter of "Amalfridam germanam suam [Theoderici]" and records her marriage to "Thuringorum regi…Herminefredo"[252].  “Theodericus rex” wrote to “Herminafrido Regi Thuringorum” granting him “ne
2 CONC ptis” in marriage[253].  Procopius records that “Hermenefrido Thoringorum regi” married "Theoderici…Amelobergam, Amalafridæ sororis suæ filiam"[254].  The Widukindi Res Gestæ Saxonicæ names "Huga rex Francorum…unicam filiam Amalbe
2 CONC rgam" who married "Irminfredo regi Thuringorum"[255].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Gregory of Tours calls Amalaberg, wife of Hermanfrid, a "wicked and cruel woman" who sowed the seeds of civil war between her husband and his brother Baderic[256].  She escaped to Ravenna with her children after the Franks attacke
2 CONC d Thuringia and killed her husband[257].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([510]) HERMANFRED, King of the Thuringians, son of --- (-534). 
2 CONT
