1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bahram died in 710, his son, Prince Khosrau (Chinese: Juluo), continued his father's military efforts. However, Khosrau's campaigns and his first successful invasion into Persia were eventually unsuccessful.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is mentionned by Arab hystorians as having accompanied the Tugesh people in their wars against the Arabs in Transoxian. While besieging Kamara in 729, Khorau tried to obtain the surrender of the Arab troops but his offer was re
2 CONC jected with contempt. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Along with most of the Sassanian imperial family who had fled their country after the Arab conquest of Persia, he lived in the area of western China. He died in China.
