1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Farrukhzad succeeded his father as the spahbed and the leader of the Pahlav (Parthian) faction, which had been formed by their father Farrukh Hormizd, who was murdered in 631.
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT Mazandaran is ruled by the Bavandid Kings until 1371, after which Seyyed Qawam al din Marashi https://www.geni.com/people/Seid-Ali-Sari-Seid-Qawam-al-din-Marashi-Governor-general-of-Mazandaran-from-1381-to-1402-Marashi-Fondateur-d
2 CONC e-la-dynastie-Alavide-%D8%B3%DB%8C%D8%AF-%D8%B9%D9%84%DB%8C-%D8%B3%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C/6000000042353375109 is governor general of Mazandaran (1381-1402). In 1408 he accepts Tamerlan's dominance.
2 CONT ======
2 CONT Farrukhzad (Middle Persian: Farrūkhzādag; New Persian: فرخزاد), was an Iranian aristocrat from the House of Ispahbudhan and the founder of the Bavand dynasty, ruling from 651 to 665. Originally a powerful servant of the Sasanian k
2 CONC ing Khosrau II (r. 590-628), he, along with several other powerful aristocrats made a conspiracy against the latter and ended his tyrannical rule. They thereafter put Khosrau's son Kavadh II (r. 628) on the throne, whose rule last
2 CONC ed only a few months, before he was killed by a plague, being succeeded by his son Ardashir III (r. 628-629), who was only after one year murdered by the rebellious former Sasanian army chief (spahbed) Shahrbaraz, who usurped the 
2 CONC throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT These events greatly weakened the Sasanian Empire, but by 632, when Khosrau's grandson Yazdegerd III (r. 632-651) ascended the throne, order was somewhat restored. However, just as peace was about to come, the Sasanian Empire was 
2 CONC invaded by Muslim Arabs, which resulted in the death of many Sasanian veterans, including Farrukhzad's brother Rostam Farrokhzad himself. Farrukhzad thereafter succeeded the latter as the spahbed and the leader of the Pahlav (Part
2 CONC hian) faction, which had been formed by their father Farrukh Hormizd, who was murdered in 631.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, Farrukhzad was unable to defeat the Arabs, and was in 643, after having seen the loss of Ctesiphon and Isfahan, Farrukhzad, along with Yazdegerd III, fled from one place to another until in 650, when Farrukhzad mutinied a
2 CONC gainst his king, who was shortly killed by one of his servants. Farrukhzad later became the ruler of Tabaristan in 651, and would rule the region until his murder in 665 by Valash, a Karenid aristocrat, who thereafter conquered hi
2 CONC s domains.
2 CONT
2 CONT The war with the Byzantines and the overthrow of Khosrau II
2 CONT The Sasanian civil war of 628-632 The Arab invasion of Iran The invasion of western Iran Flight to Khorasan, rule and death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Farrukhzad was the son of Farrukh Hormizd, a prominent aristocrat from the Ispahbudhan family, who served as the army chief (spahbed) of the kusts of Adurbadagan and Khorasan—he was one of the generals who led the Sasanian army du
2 CONC ring the Byzantine–Sasanian War of 602–628, but in 626 along with his comrade Shahrbaraz rebelled against the Sasanian king Khosrau II (r. 590-628).
2 CONT
2 CONT Farrukhzad had one brother named Rostam Farrokhzad, who at that time resided in the Adurbadagan province
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Farrukhzad (Middle Persian: Farrūkhzādag; New Persian: فرخزاد), was an Iranian aristocrat from the House of Ispahbudhan and the founder of the Bavand dynasty, ruling from 651 to 665. Originally a powerful servant of the Sasanian k
2 CONC ing Khosrow II (r. 590-628), he, along with several other powerful aristocrats made a conspiracy against the latter and ended his tyrannical rule. They thereafter put Khosrow's son Kavadh II (r. 628) on the throne, whose rule last
2 CONC ed only a few months, before he was killed by a plague, being succeeded by his son Ardashir III (r. 628-629), who was only after one year murdered by the rebellious former Sasanian army chief (spahbed) Shahrbaraz, who usurped the 
2 CONC throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT These events greatly weakened the Sasanian Empire, but by 632, when Khosrow's grandson Yazdegerd III (r. 632-651) ascended the throne, order was somewhat restored. However, just as peace was about to come, the Sasanian Empire was 
2 CONC invaded by Muslim Arabs, which resulted in the death of many Sasanian veterans, including Farrukhzad's brother Rostam Farrokhzad himself. Farrukhzad thereafter succeeded the latter as the spahbed and the leader of the Pahlav (Part
2 CONC hian) faction, which had been formed by their father Farrukh Hormizd, who was murdered in 631.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, Farrukhzad was unable to defeat the Arabs, and was in 643, after having seen the loss of Ctesiphon and Spahan, Farrukhzad, along with Yazdegerd III, fled[clarify] from one place to another until in 650, when Farrukhzad mu
2 CONC tinied against his king, who was shortly killed by one of his servants. Farrukhzad later became the ruler of Tabaristan in 651, and would rule the region until his murder in 665 by Valash, a Karenid aristocrat, who thereafter conq
2 CONC uered his domains.[1]
