1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''THORISMUND (-killed in battle [451/55])
2 CONT '''s/o HUNIMUND 
2 CONT *BERIMUD 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HUNGARY.htm#_Toc146273201
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thorismund Thorismund From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Thorismund (Gothic: Þaurismoþs, also Thorismod or Thorismud, as manuscripts of our chief source confusingly attest[1]), (c. 420 – 453) becam
2 CONC e king of the Visigoths after his father Theodoric was killed in the Battle of Châlons in 451 CE. He was murdered in 453 and was succeeded by his brother Theodoric II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorismund appears to have played a pivotal role in the Battle of Châlons as he led a contingent of the Visigoth forces into capturing an important summit at the very early stages of the conflict. The summit seems to have extended
2 CONC  to the whole of the left flank of the Ostrogoth and Hun forces. Thorismund descended from the hills during the late stages of the conflict, when the Huns had prevailed over the Alans, and the Ostrogoths were pushing the disorgani
2 CONC zed Visigoths after the death of their king Theodoric. Thorismund led his force of Visigoths in a decisive charge which, according to Gibbon, flanked both the Ostrogoths and subsequently the Huns and snatched the victory from his 
2 CONC enemies.
2 CONT
2 CONT References[edit] Jump up ^ Jordanes, De origine actibusque Getarum (Getica) 81, 174, 190, 201 and elsewhere. External links[edit]
2 CONT  Media related to Turismundo at Wikimedia Commons
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Gibbon, History of the Decline and Fall of the Roman Empire, chapter 35 .....>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Hungary:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HUNGARY.htm#_Toc146273199
2 CONT
2 CONT HUNIMUND (Ostrogoth Generation 11)
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Hunimundum" as son of "Hermanaricus"[40]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT THORISMUND (-killed in battle [451/55], Ostrogoth Generation 12)  
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Thorismundo" as son of "Hunimundus"[41].  Iordanes records that "Thorismundo filius eius" succeeded as King of the Goths after the death of "Hunimundus filius quondam regis…Hermanarici" but was killed fighting the 
2 CONC Gepids in the second year of his reign[42]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT BERIMUD (Ostrogoth Generation 13)
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Berimud" as son of "Thorismundo"[43].  Iordanes records that "Beremud…cum filio Vitiricho" left the Ostrogoths to join "Vallia rex Gothorum" [King of the Visigoths in Toulouse][44].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The implication of a later passage in Iordanes, which records that "Valamer…ex consobrino eius genitus Vandalario" succeeded as king after "Thorismundo" was killed[45], is that Berimud's departure was triggered after he was passed
2 CONC  over in the succession. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT [40] Iordanes Getarum, MGH Auct. ant. V.1, p. 77. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [41] Iordanes Getarum, MGH Auct. ant. V.1, p. 77. 
