2 CONT Merovech/Merowig (411-457) (Latin: Meroveus or Merovius; French: Mérovée) is the legendary founder of the Merovingian dynasty of the Salian Franks, which later became the dominant Frankish tribe. The name is a Latinization of a fo
2 CONC rm close to Old High German proper name Marwig, lit. "famed fight"[1] (cf. māri "famous" + wīg "fight").
