2 CONT MEROVIUS, KING OF THE SALIC FRANKS
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 411 A.D.; d. 458 A.D.
2 CONT
2 CONT Merovius gave the name to his descendants and his dynasty. Merovius had one recorded son: Childeric, b. 436 A.D. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Merovech is possibly the son of Clodio (born 395, died 447-449).  Clodio was known as "The Long-haired" or "Hairy."  He was the son of Argotta (the son of Gerrobaud) and Pharamond (the daughter of Marcomer).  There is a legend tha
2 CONC t Marcomer was the son of the legendary Priam, who is known as the father of Laomedan (a Trojan King), who is known in the legend as the father of Ilus, the King of Troy during the Trojan War.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Seimi-legendary early Frankish King for whom the Merovingian Dynasty is named (Meroveus in Latin). His whole line was characterized by long hair as a symbol of royalty. He fought against the Visigoths under the Roman General Aetiu
2 CONC s at the Battle of Chalons in 451. Name also seen as: Meroveus Salic & Merovech.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT The book, 'Kings & Queens of Europe'
2 CONT
2 CONT The book, 'The Dark Ages'
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Merovaeus, founder of the Merovingian House of Frankish Kings, was possibly the son-in-law rather than son of
2 CONT
2 CONT Clodion. Merovaeus defeated Atilla with the aid of Aetius in 451 and reigned as King, 448-458. Also known as
2 CONT
2 CONT Merowig, he was a Flandrian or Tournai Frank.{See Encyclopaedia Brit., 1959, 5:467-8, 9:698}
2 CONT
2 CONT Merovaeus (Meroveus/Merovee/Merovech) was King of the Salian Franks from 447 to 456, after whom the Merovingian Dynasty is named. It is believed by some historians that this dynasty was descended from Jesus and Mary Magdalene, and
2 CONC  that the blood-line has continued down through the centuries to the present day. Organisations which seem to been involved in its continuation and protection include the Knights Templar and the 'secret society', The Priory of Sio
2 CONC n, whose Grand Masters are said to include Leonardo da Vinci, Isaac Newton, Victor Hugo and Claude Debussy.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Defeated Attila the Hun in 458.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Roi des Francs Saliens de 448 à 457.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contre l'opinion généralement admise, qui fait de Mérovée le fils de Chlodion le Chevelu, Gilles Houdry pense qu'il n'en était que le gendre.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Merovee, King of the Franks from 447-458 A.D., was an adherent of the cult of Diana. His Son,
2 CONT
2 CONT Childeric I, 458-481 A.D, practiced witchcraft (Paganism). His son, Clovis I, 481-511 A.D., adopted
2 CONT
2 CONT christianity in 496 A.D.
2 CONT
2 CONT    *In 496 A.D., the Bishop of Rome made a pact with Clovis, the Grandson of Merovee, King of the
2 CONT
2 CONT Franks, calling him "The New Constantine", giving him authority to preside over a "Christianized
2 CONT
2 CONT Roman Empire". (The term "Holy Roman Empire" was not officially used until 962 A.D.)
2 CONT
2 CONT (bk-4,11-13)  At this time the church was not yet aware of the Merovingian connection.
2 CONT
2 CONT    *Rev. J.R. Church, author of "Guardians of the Grail", traces the lineage of these Merovingian
2 CONT
2 CONT Kings and documents that most European royalty descends from this bloodline, including the
2 CONT
2 CONT Hapsburg dynasty and the present royalty of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT    *Clovis was suceeded by his son Dagobert II, born in 651. Clovis ruled the Franks and Gauls from
2 CONT
2 CONT France and died when Dagobert was age 5. A struggle broke out for ascendancy to the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5-year old Dagobert was reported to have been killed. But, in fact he was kidnapped by a catholic
2 CONT
2 CONT priest and spirited away to Ireland where he was raised and protected at the Irish Monastary of
2 CONT
2 CONT Slane, not far from Dublin, and here at the school attached to the monastary, he recieved an
2 CONT
2 CONT education unobtainable in France at the time. (bk-1,247)
2 CONT
2 CONT    *In 666, Dagobert II married a Celtic Princess, fathering three daughters but no sons. Soon he
2 CONT
2 CONT moved to England establishing residence at York. His first wife died in 670 A.D. and Dagobert II
2 CONT
2 CONT returned to France. He married his second wife, Giselle de Razes, daughter of the Count of Razes
2 CONT
2 CONT and niece of the King of the Visigoths in southern France. The marriage was celebrated at Rennes le
2 CONT
2 CONT Chateau, a Visigoth bastion, the same village where Saunier found the secret genealogies in 1891.
2 CONT
2 CONT With this marriage, the Merovingian bloodline was now allied with the Royal bloodline of the
2 CONT
2 CONT Visigoths, who had strong gnostic tendencies. Dagobert II was in fact converted to the religion by his
2 CONT
2 CONT wife, turning away from his catholic heritage.
2 CONT
2 CONT      Finally, in 674, with the support of his mother and her advisors, the long exiled monarch
2 CONT
2 CONT announced who he was, reclaimed his realm and was officially proclaimed King of Austrisia, which
2 CONT
2 CONT took in the territory of North-Western Europe and parts of what are now Austria and Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT (bk-1,250)
2 CONT
2 CONT    *Dagobert II established a Coat-Of-Arms for Rennes le Chateau consisting of two triangles
2 CONT
2 CONT interlaced, one, white and upright and the other black and upside down, forming a six-pointed star.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is a dominant symbol in Freemasonry. (bk-1,396)
2 CONT
2 CONT    *Mackey's "Encyclopedia of Freemasonry" defines the six-pointed star as representing the good
2 CONT
2 CONT and evil powers in life. (bk-6)
2 CONT
2 CONT    *Dagobert II set himself against the Roman church and by this time Rome was knowledgable
2 CONT
2 CONT about the Merovingian "Heresay".
2 CONT
2 CONT    *On Dec. 3,679, while resting under a tree during a hunt in the Ardenes Forest in northern France,
2 CONT
2 CONT Dagobert II was assassinated. The murderers then returned to his northern palace intent on
2 CONT
2 CONT exterminating the rest of the Royal family. (bk-2,52)
2 CONT
