1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Frankish_queens List of Frankish queens] From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is a list of the women who have been Queens consort of the Frankish people. As all monarchs of the Franks have been required by law and tradition to be male, there has never been a Queen regnant of the Franks (although some w
2 CONC omen have governed as regents).
2 CONT
2 CONT A timeline of consorts Frankish rulers is difficult since the realm was, according to old Germanic practice, frequently divided among the sons of a leader upon his death and then eventually reunited. Another factor is the practice
2 CONC  of polygamy in the Frankish society, and it is unclear who was a concubine, a mistress, or a legal wife. Most of early Merovingian queens are nothing but names, and almost nothing is known about them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Merovingian dynasty (450–751)
2 CONT
2 CONT The marital status of some wives of early Frankish kings are unclear and polygamy was practiced.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Evochildis''' ("Of Cologne")	? Princesa Franco-renana (Probably a Franco-Rhenish Princess; likely mother of Theuderic I)[1][clarification needed].  Married Clovis l in 484.  ['''source for name needed'''] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. [https://wc.rootsweb.com/trees/162017/P725/evochildis-decologne/individual “ The Painter & Woods Families of Fulton Co, Illinois”] Rootsweb. [https://wiki2.org/en/Theuderic_I a.] ''Continued'': He (Theuderic I) was the son of C
2 CONC lovis I and one of his earlier wives or concubines (possibly a Franco-Rhenish Princess, Evochildis of Cologne[2]). 
2 CONT ** 2. Wood 1994, p. 50
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT THEODERICH ([485]-end 533, bur Metz). Gregory of Tours names Theoderich as son of King Clovis by '''one of his mistresses''', born before his marriage to Clotilde[55]. "Theodorico, Chlomiro, Hildeberto, Hlodario" are named (in ord
2 CONC er) as sons of "Chlodoveus" in the Regum Merowingorum Genealogia
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Theuderic I[a] (c. 485 – 533/4) was the Merovingian king of Metz, Rheims, or Austrasia—as it is variously called—from 511 to 533 or 534.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
