2 CONC on of Childerich & Basina[37].   … '''[married firstly] ---, daughter of --- [of the Franks of the Rhine].''' According to Gregory of Tours, the mother of Theoderich was one of King Clovis's concubines not his first wife[46].  Set
2 CONC tipani[47] suggests that Theoderich’s mother was a Frank from the Rhine region, based on the inheritance of Austrasia by Theoderich and the roots "Theode-" and "-rich" in his name, possibly transmitted through his mother from Theo
2 CONC demer and Richomer who were both 4th century Frankish kings.  married  [secondly] (492) CHROTECHILDIS [Clotilde/Rotilde[48]] of Burgundy, daughter of CHILPERICH King of Burgundy & his wife''' ([480] …
