2 CONT >>>>>d)         [CHROTIELDIS [Clotilde] ([after 561]-after 590).  Gregory of Tours records that Clotilde, who "used to pretend that she was Charibert's daughter" (which suggests doubt about the correctness of her assertion), led a
2 CONC  revolt in the convent of Sainte-Croix in Poitiers, together with Basina daughter of King Chilperich, against abbess Leubovera[189].  She was excommunicated for involvement in political intrigue, but accepted back at her convent. 
2 CONC  If Chrotieldis was the daughter of King Charibert, no indication has been found concerning the identity of her mother.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>4.         GUNTCHRAMN [Gontran] ([532/34]-28 Mar 592, bur basilique Saint-Marcel, near Chalon-sur-Saône).  Gregory of Tours names (in order) Gunthar, Childerich, Charibert, Guntram, Sigibert and a daughter Clothsind as the chi
2 CONC ldren of King Clotaire and his wife Ingonde[190].  He succeeded his father in 561 as GONTRAN King of the Franks, his territories covering those previously held by his uncle King Chlodomer, with Orléans as his capital[191].  The Ma
2 CONC rii Episcopi Aventicensis Chronica records that "filii ipsius Charibertus, Guntegramnus, Hilpericus et Sigibertus" divided the kingdom between them on the death of their father in 561[192].  He adopted his nephew King Childebert I
2 CONC I as his successor in 577, the arrangement being renewed under the treaty of Andelot dated 28 Nov 587[193].  Fredegar records the death of King Guntram "anno 33 regni…V Kal Apr" and his burial "in ecclesia sancti Marcelli" in the 
2 CONC monastery which he had built[194].  m firstly ([556]) MARCATRUDIS, daughter of MAGNACHAR Duke of the Transjuranian Franks & his wife --- (-after [556]).  Gregory of Tours names Marcatrude, daughter of Magnachar, as the wife of Kin
2 CONC g Gontran, specifying that she poisoned her stepson Gundobald but died soon after her own son[195].  m secondly (566) AUSTRECHILDIS [Bobilla], daughter of --- ([548]-Sep 580).  Gregory of Tours names Austrechild "also called Bobil
2 CONC la" as the second wife of King Gontran[196].  She was a servant in the household of his first wife's father.  Gregory of Tours records the death of Queen Austrechild, specifying that "this wicked woman" requested as a dying wish t
2 CONC hat the two doctors who had unsuccessfully treated her should have their throats cut[197].  An epitaph to “Austrigildis Reginæ” refers to her as “Regum genetrix et Regia conjunx”[198].  The record of the Council of Valence dated 2
2 CONC 2 Jun 585 names “Guntramni Regis…bonæ memoriæ iugalis sua Austrechildis regina vel filiæ eorum Deo sacratæ puellæ…bonæ memoriæ Clodeberga vel Clodehildis”[199].  Mistress (1): (before [549]) VENERANDA, daughter of ---.  Gregory of
2 CONC  Tours names Veneranda, servant of one of his subjects, as the mistress of King Gontran before his first marriage[200].  >>>>King Gontran & his first wife had one child:
