2 CONT >>>>>b)         CHLOTHACHAR [Clotaire] ([567]-577 or before).  Gregory of Tours names (in order) Clotaire and Chlodomer as the two sons of King Gontran & his second wife but refers to him as having been "left childless" in a later
2 CONC  passage which records that he adopted his nephew King Childebert II as his heir[202].  The Marii Episcopi Aventicensis Chronica records the death in 577 of "regis atque egregii adolescente Chlothacarius et Chlodomeris filii Gunth
2 CONC egramni regis"[203].  An epitaph is written in honour of “Clotharii fratris Chlodomeri”[204]. 
