2 CONT >>>>>c)         CHLODOMER (-577 or before).  Gregory of Tours names (in order) Lothar and Chlodomer as the two sons of King Gontran & his second wife but refers to him as having been "left childless" in a later passage which recor
2 CONC ds that he adopted his nephew King Childebert II as his heir[205].  The Marii Episcopi Aventicensis Chronica records the death in 577 of "regis atque egregii adolescente Chlothacarius et Chlodomeris filii Gunthegramni regis"[206].
2 CONC   An epitaph is written in honour of “Chlodomeri filii Guntchramni Regis”[207]. 
