2 CONT >>>>>f)          GUNDOBALD ([549]-after [556]).  Gregory of Tours names Gundobad as son of King Gontran and his mistress Veneranda, specifying that his father sent him to Orléans and that he was poisoned by his stepmother Queen Ma
2 CONC rcatrudis[211].    
