2 CONT
2 CONT [3] Thorpe, L. (trans.) (1974) Gregory of Tours: The History of the Franks (Penguin), ("Gregory of Tours") II.28, p. 141. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [4] Chronicle of 511, 689 and 690, cited in Wood (1994), p. 48. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [5] Wood (1994), p. 52. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [53] Marii Episcopi Aventicensis Chronica 516, MGH Auct. ant. XI, p. 234. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [54] Gregory of Tours III.5, p. 165. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [55] Wood, I. (1994) The Merovingian Kingdoms (Longman), pp. 51-2. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [56] Wolfram, H. (1998) History Of The Goths (Berkeley, California), p. 312. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [57] Wolfram (1998), p. 313.  The conversion must have taken place before 514, when Pope Symachus died. 
2 CONT
