1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''VANDALARIUS'''
2 CONT s/o VINITHARIUS
2 CONT * VALAMIR (-killed in battle [468/69]).
2 CONT *THEODEMIR [Thiudimir] (-Kyrrhos 474) -        KINGS of ITALY. 
2 CONT *VIDIMIR (-473)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Hungary:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HUNGARY.htm#VandalariusA
2 CONT
2 CONT VINITHARIUS .  Iordanes names "Vinitharius" as the son of Valaravans[37]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VANDALARIUS, son of VINITHARIUS .  Iordanes names "Vandiliarum" as son of "Vinitharius" and father of "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir"[52].  Relative of Thorismund[53]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. VALAMIR (-killed in battle [468/69]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir" as the sons of Vandilarius[54].  He and his brothers followed Attila the Hun into Gaul in 451[55].  Valamir commanded the Ostrogoth contingent in Attila's army which was defeated at
2 CONC  the battle of the Catalaunian fields[56].  He was considered king of all Ostrogoths in Pannonia.  Iordanes records that "Valamer…ex consobrino eius genitus Vandalario" succeeded as king after "Thorismundo" was killed fighting the
2 CONC  Gepids in the second year of his reign[57].  He shared the land with his two brothers, retaining for himself the eastern part of the territory covering lower Slavonia.  In 456, he defeated an attack by the Huns, who are said to h
2 CONC ave retreated to the River Dnieper[58].  He defeated another Hun attack on Bassianae, near Belgrade, in 467/68, but was killed in battle during a similar attack the following year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. THEODEMIR [Thiudimir] (-Kyrrhos 474).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir" as the sons of Vandilarius[59].  King of the Ostrogoths in Pannonia, subordinate to his brother Valamir, he ruled over the western part of their domain which covered the county of S
2 CONC omogy and north-eastern Croatia.  He succeeded his brother in [468/49] as King of all the Pannonian Ostrogoths.  Iordanes names "Theodemir" when recording that he succeeded his brother "Valamero rege Gothorum" together with "Vidim
2 CONC ero fratre et filio Theodorico"[60].  When the Ostrogoths left Pannonia in [473], Theodemir and his contingent went towards Constantinople.  They settled in Macedonia, based in the city of Kyrrhos[61]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. VIDIMIR (-473).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir" as the sons of Vandilarius[62].  King of the Ostrogoths in Pannonia, subordinate to his brother Valamir, he ruled over the central part of their domain which covered upper Slavonia.
2 CONC   Iordanes names "Theodemir" when recording that he succeeded his brother "Valamero rege Gothorum" together with "Vidimero fratre et filio Theodorico"[63].  When the Ostrogoths left Pannonia in [473], Vidimir went into Italy where
2 CONC  he suffered several defeats. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Vandalarius (who was never King of the Ostrogoths) is identified in the "Origin and Deeds of the Goths" by Jordanes/Iordanes, which is featured on the Boudicca's Bard website:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.boudicca.de/jordanes4-e.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT (The Divided Goths: Ostrogoths)
2 CONT
2 CONT XLVIII
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT (250) And later, after the death of Vinitharius, Hunimund ruled them, the son of Hermanaric, a mighty king of yore; a man fierce in war and of famous personal beauty, who afterwards fought successfully against the race of the Suav
2 CONC i. And when he died, his son Thorismud succeeded him, in the very bloom of youth. In the second year of his rule he moved an army against the Gepidae and won a great victory over them, but is said to have been killed by falling fr
2 CONC om his horse.
2 CONT
2 CONT (251) When he was dead, the Ostrogoths mourned for him so deeply that for 40 years no other king succeeded in his place, and during all this time they had ever on their lips the tale of his memory. Now as time went on, Valamir gre
2 CONC w to man's estate. He was the son of Thorismud's cousin Vandalarius. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------- 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Thomas Hodgkin in "Theodoric the Goth: The Barbarian Champion of Civilisation", Cassiodorus, Secretary of Ostrogoth King Theodoric the Great, gave Vinitharius, Vandalarius' father, the epithet of "The Just" rather tha
2 CONC n "The Conqueror". Source: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.gutenberg.org/files/20063/20063-h/20063-h.htm#p7 
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT According to "Bert's Geschiedenis Site":
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.bertsgeschiedenissite.nl/ijzertijd/eeuw4ac/ostrogoten.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Vandalarius died in 459 (no source given). If he had done so, then he likely would have followed his sons to Pannonia. But there is nothing that confirms either date or place in contemporary literature. (And certainly there is not
2 CONC hing that confirms him fighting the Vandals - any contact with the Vandals would have likely been with the Visigoths under the House of Balti.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Wandalar (Vandalarius) (ca. 400 - 459) (= overwinnaar van de Vandalen), de zoon van Winithar. Hij stierf in 459.
2 CONT
2 CONT Toen na de dood van Hunnenkoning Attila in 453 een opvolgingsstrijd losbarstte kwamen de Gepiden onder hun koning  Ardaric tegen hun vroegere onderdrukkers in opstand. De Ostrogoten, aangevoerd door de drie zonen van Wandalar Thiu
2 CONC dimir, Valamir en Vidimir sloten zich bij deze opstand aan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In de slag aan de Nadao (454), een zijrivier van de Sava, ergens in Pannonia, werden de Hunnen en hun bondgenoten (Sarmaten en Alanen) verslagen. Door deze overwinning kwam er een einde aan de overheersing van de Hunnen in Centraa
2 CONC l en Oostelijk Europa. De Ostrogoten herkregen hun vrijheid en werden bondgenoten van het Oost-Romeinse Rijk, dat hen in ruil hiervoor in 455 de voormalige provincie Pannonia als woongebied toewees. Niet lang na de overwinning op 
2 CONC de Hunnen kwam de oude rivaliteit tussen de Gepiden en Ostrogoten weer boven drijven. Er ontstonden voortdurend schermutselingen tussen deze volken waarbij ook de Skiren en Herulen betrokken waren. Pas in 469 kwam hier een einde a
2 CONC an toen de Ostrogoten de Gepiden uit Pannonia verdreven.
2 CONT
2 CONT In English:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wanadalar (Vandalarius, c.400-459, "The Conqueror of the Vandals") was the son of Winithar. He died in 459.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of their King Attila in 453 (presumably meaning the overlordship imposed upon them by the Huns), a succession struggle broke out among the Gepids under their King Ardaric as he led a rebellion against their former 
2 CONC oppressors. The Ostrogoths, led by three sons of Wandalar, Thiudimir, Valamar, and Vidimir, joined this rebellion. (Most sources indicate this was a rebellion carried out spontaneously among several tribes, following the weakening
2 CONC  of Attila after the Battle of the Catalaunian Fields near Chalons in 451.)
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Battle of Nadao (454), a tributary of the Sava located somewhere in Pannonia, the Huns and their allies (Sarmatians and Alans) were reportedly defeated. This victory brought to an end the domination of the Huns in Central a
2 CONC nd Eastern Europe. The Ostroogths regained their freedom and became allies of the Eastern Roman Empire, who gave them in return the Roman province of Pannonia as a homeland in 455 (more or less, this was a confirmation of their ho
2 CONC meland, given somewhat later as a result of a struggle with a rival over who would represent the Ostrogoths in Constantinople). Not long after the victory over the Huns, the old rivalry between the Gepids and the Ostrogoths came b
2 CONC ack to the surface. There were constant skirmishes between the nations where the Sciri and Heruli were involved (this would apparently be the conflict that killed his son Valamar). Only in 469 did the war come to an end when the O
2 CONC strogoths and Gepids of Pannonia were displaced. (This war actually continued after their displacement, when Theodoric fought and defeated Odoacer, a Sciri Goth, in Italy.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Obtenido de: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vandalario
2 CONT
2 CONT Vandalario fue un caudillo ostrogodo que sometió a los vándalos. Fue hijo de un tal Vinitharius, conquistador de los vénetos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fue padre de los tres líderes que llevaron a los ostrogodos a liberarse de los hunos: Teodomiro, Valamiro y Videmiro por tanto abuelo de Teodorico I el Grande, hijo de Teodomiro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vandalario murió en 459
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Hungary:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HUNGARY.htm#VandalariusA
2 CONT
2 CONT VINITHARIUS . Iordanes names "Vinitharius" as the son of Valaravans[37].
2 CONT
2 CONT VANDALARIUS, son of VINITHARIUS . Iordanes names "Vandiliarum" as son of "Vinitharius" and father of "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir"[52]. Relative of Thorismund[53].
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. VALAMIR (-killed in battle [468/69]).
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir" as the sons of Vandilarius[54]. He and his brothers followed Attila the Hun into Gaul in 451[55]. Valamir commanded the Ostrogoth contingent in Attila's army which was defeated at t
2 CONC he battle of the Catalaunian fields[56]. He was considered king of all Ostrogoths in Pannonia. Iordanes records that "Valamer…ex consobrino eius genitus Vandalario" succeeded as king after "Thorismundo" was killed fighting the Gep
2 CONC ids in the second year of his reign[57]. He shared the land with his two brothers, retaining for himself the eastern part of the territory covering lower Slavonia. In 456, he defeated an attack by the Huns, who are said to have re
2 CONC treated to the River Dnieper[58]. He defeated another Hun attack on Bassianae, near Belgrade, in 467/68, but was killed in battle during a similar attack the following year.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. THEODEMIR [Thiudimir] (-Kyrrhos 474).
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir" as the sons of Vandilarius[59]. King of the Ostrogoths in Pannonia, subordinate to his brother Valamir, he ruled over the western part of their domain which covered the county of So
2 CONC mogy and north-eastern Croatia. He succeeded his brother in [468/49] as King of all the Pannonian Ostrogoths. Iordanes names "Theodemir" when recording that he succeeded his brother "Valamero rege Gothorum" together with "Vidimero
2 CONC  fratre et filio Theodorico"[60]. When the Ostrogoths left Pannonia in [473], Theodemir and his contingent went towards Constantinople. They settled in Macedonia, based in the city of Kyrrhos[61].
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. VIDIMIR (-473).
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir" as the sons of Vandilarius[62]. King of the Ostrogoths in Pannonia, subordinate to his brother Valamir, he ruled over the central part of their domain which covered upper Slavonia. 
2 CONC Iordanes names "Theodemir" when recording that he succeeded his brother "Valamero rege Gothorum" together with "Vidimero fratre et filio Theodorico"[63]. When the Ostrogoths left Pannonia in [473], Vidimir went into Italy where he
2 CONC  suffered several defeats.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Vandalarius (who was never King of the Ostrogoths) is identified in the "Origin and Deeds of the Goths" by Jordanes/Iordanes, which is featured on the Boudicca's Bard website:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.boudicca.de/jordanes4-e.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT (The Divided Goths: Ostrogoths)
2 CONT
2 CONT XLVIII
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT (250) And later, after the death of Vinitharius, Hunimund ruled them, the son of Hermanaric, a mighty king of yore; a man fierce in war and of famous personal beauty, who afterwards fought successfully against the race of the Suav
2 CONC i. And when he died, his son Thorismud succeeded him, in the very bloom of youth. In the second year of his rule he moved an army against the Gepidae and won a great victory over them, but is said to have been killed by falling fr
2 CONC om his horse.
2 CONT
2 CONT (251) When he was dead, the Ostrogoths mourned for him so deeply that for 40 years no other king succeeded in his place, and during all this time they had ever on their lips the tale of his memory. Now as time went on, Valamir gre
2 CONC w to man's estate. He was the son of Thorismud's cousin Vandalarius.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Thomas Hodgkin in "Theodoric the Goth: The Barbarian Champion of Civilisation", Cassiodorus, Secretary of Ostrogoth King Theodoric the Great, gave Vinitharius, Vandalarius' father, the epithet of "The Just" rather tha
2 CONC n "The Conqueror". Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.gutenberg.org/files/20063/20063-h/20063-h.htm#p7
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT According to "Bert's Geschiedenis Site":
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.bertsgeschiedenissite.nl/ijzertijd/eeuw4ac/ostrogoten.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Vandalarius died in 459 (no source given). If he had done so, then he likely would have followed his sons to Pannonia. But there is nothing that confirms either date or place in contemporary literature. (And certainly there is not
2 CONC hing that confirms him fighting the Vandals - any contact with the Vandals would have likely been with the Visigoths under the House of Balti.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Wandalar (Vandalarius) (ca. 400 - 459) (= overwinnaar van de Vandalen), de zoon van Winithar. Hij stierf in 459.
2 CONT
2 CONT Toen na de dood van Hunnenkoning Attila in 453 een opvolgingsstrijd losbarstte kwamen de Gepiden onder hun koning Ardaric tegen hun vroegere onderdrukkers in opstand. De Ostrogoten, aangevoerd door de drie zonen van Wandalar Thiud
2 CONC imir, Valamir en Vidimir sloten zich bij deze opstand aan.
2 CONT
2 CONT In de slag aan de Nadao (454), een zijrivier van de Sava, ergens in Pannonia, werden de Hunnen en hun bondgenoten (Sarmaten en Alanen) verslagen. Door deze overwinning kwam er een einde aan de overheersing van de Hunnen in Centraa
2 CONC l en Oostelijk Europa. De Ostrogoten herkregen hun vrijheid en werden bondgenoten van het Oost-Romeinse Rijk, dat hen in ruil hiervoor in 455 de voormalige provincie Pannonia als woongebied toewees. Niet lang na de overwinning op 
2 CONC de Hunnen kwam de oude rivaliteit tussen de Gepiden en Ostrogoten weer boven drijven. Er ontstonden voortdurend schermutselingen tussen deze volken waarbij ook de Skiren en Herulen betrokken waren. Pas in 469 kwam hier een einde a
2 CONC an toen de Ostrogoten de Gepiden uit Pannonia verdreven.
2 CONT
2 CONT In English:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wanadalar (Vandalarius, c.400-459, "The Conqueror of the Vandals") was the son of Winithar. He died in 459.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of their King Attila in 453 (presumably meaning the overlordship imposed upon them by the Huns), a succession struggle broke out among the Gepids under their King Ardaric as he led a rebellion against their former 
2 CONC oppressors. The Ostrogoths, led by three sons of Wandalar, Thiudimir, Valamar, and Vidimir, joined this rebellion. (Most sources indicate this was a rebellion carried out spontaneously among several tribes, following the weakening
2 CONC  of Attila after the Battle of the Catalaunian Fields near Chalons in 451.)
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Battle of Nadao (454), a tributary of the Sava located somewhere in Pannonia, the Huns and their allies (Sarmatians and Alans) were reportedly defeated. This victory brought to an end the domination of the Huns in Central a
2 CONC nd Eastern Europe. The Ostroogths regained their freedom and became allies of the Eastern Roman Empire, who gave them in return the Roman province of Pannonia as a homeland in 455 (more or less, this was a confirmation of their ho
2 CONC meland, given somewhat later as a result of a struggle with a rival over who would represent the Ostrogoths in Constantinople). Not long after the victory over the Huns, the old rivalry between the Gepids and the Ostrogoths came b
2 CONC ack to the surface. There were constant skirmishes between the nations where the Sciri and Heruli were involved (this would apparently be the conflict that killed his son Valamar). Only in 469 did the war come to an end when the O
2 CONC strogoths and Gepids of Pannonia were displaced. (This war actually continued after their displacement, when Theodoric fought and defeated Odoacer, a Sciri Goth, in Italy.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Obtenido de:
2 CONT
