1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''VIDIMIR''' (-473) king of all Ostrogoths in Pannonia
2 CONT s/o VANDALARIUS
2 CONT *   VIDIMIR
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HUNGARY.htm#_Toc146273199
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT VANDALARIUS, son of VINITHARIUS (Ostrogoth Generation 12)
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Vandiliarum" as son of "Vinitharius" and father of "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir"[52].  Relative of Thorismund[53]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VALAMIR (-killed in battle [468/69], Ostrogoth Generation 13).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir" as the sons of Vandilarius[54].  He and his brothers followed Attila the Hun into Gaul in 451[55].  Valamir commanded the Ostrogoth contingent in Attila's army which was defeated at
2 CONC  the battle of the Catalaunian fields[56].  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was considered king of all Ostrogoths in Pannonia.  Iordanes records that "Valamer…ex consobrino eius genitus Vandalario" succeeded as king after "Thorismundo" was killed fighting the Gepids in the second year of his reign[57].
2 CONC   He shared the land with his two brothers, retaining for himself the eastern part of the territory covering lower Slavonia.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 456, he defeated an attack by the Huns, who are said to have retreated to the River Dnieper[58].  
2 CONT
2 CONT He defeated another Hun attack on Bassianae, near Belgrade, in 467/68, but was killed in battle during a similar attack the following year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. THEODEMIR [Thiudimir] (-Kyrrhos 474, Ostrogoth Generation 13).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir" as the sons of Vandilarius[59].  
2 CONT
2 CONT King of the Ostrogoths in Pannonia, subordinate to his brother Valamir, he ruled over the western part of their domain which covered the county of Somogy and north-eastern Croatia.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his brother in [468/49] as King of all the Pannonian Ostrogoths. Iordanes names "Theodemir" when recording that he succeeded his brother "Valamero rege Gothorum" together with "Vidimero fratre et filio Theodorico"[60]
2 CONC .  
2 CONT
2 CONT When the Ostrogoths left Pannonia in [473], Theodemir and his contingent went towards Constantinople.  They settled in Macedonia, based in the city of Kyrrhos[61]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.  VIDIMIR (-473, Ostrogoth Generation 13). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Thiudemer et Valamir et Vidimir" as the sons of Vandilarius[62].  
2 CONT
2 CONT King of the Ostrogoths in Pannonia, subordinate to his brother Valamir, he ruled over the central part of their domain which covered upper Slavonia.  Iordanes names "Theodemir" when recording that he succeeded his brother "Valamer
2 CONC o rege Gothorum" together with "Vidimero fratre et filio Theodorico"[63].  
2 CONT
2 CONT When the Ostrogoths left Pannonia in [473], Vidimir went into Italy where he suffered several defeats. 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)  VIDIMIR (Ostrogoth Generation 14)
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes records that "Vidimero cum Vidimero filio" were sent to "partes Hesperias" by Theodemir[64].  
2 CONT
2 CONT After his father's death, Emperor Glycerius sent Vidimir and his contingent of Pannonian Ostrogoths to Gaul, where he settled in the Limousin[65]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
