2 CONT Anonymous, d. c.500
2 CONT
2 CONT First husband of Amalafrida, the sister of Theodoricus. He was the father of Theodahadus and of Amalaberga, hence grandfather of Amalafridas, Theudegisclus and Theudenantha. He was presumably not one of Theodoric's many diplomatic
2 CONC  family alliances, since Theodahad was already an adult by 507/511, so the marriage had probably taken place before Theodoric and his family came to Italy. He was therefore presumably someone from the Balkans, who probably identif
2 CONC ied himself as a goth, and who probably had a Germanic name (since no Latin name appears among his children or grandchildren). Given the possible dates, Amalafrida might have married him upon her return to Theodoric from the retin
2 CONC ue of the Empress Ariadne in c.487 (on this event, see PLRE2: 63 and Wolfram, Goths, p.278.
