1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irbis_(Khazar)
2 CONT
2 CONT Irbis (fl. 650 or 652) was according to a number of Russian sources the founder of the Khazar Khaganate. The Khazars traced their origin to the Turkic Ashina clan in modern Mongolia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Golden notes that Chinese and Arabic reports are almost identical, making the connection a strong one, and conjectures that Khazar leader may have been Irbis Seguy, who lost power or was killed around 651.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Irbis is the name of the first khagan to rule over a unified Khazar Khaganate in the middle of the seventh century. Irbis is described as a scion of the Göktürk royal house, the Ashina, and specifically as a son or near kinsman of
2 CONC  Tong Yabghu Khagan (Ziebel), a khagan of the Western Göktürks.
