1 NOTE Source: THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry, chart page 61.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 65:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.   CLODION, c.380-448 A.D., legendary King of the Salic Franks from 428.  His lands were at Tournai corresponding general to the territory of Hainaut.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amy, Adam and FAL.
1 NOTE [FAVthomas.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Frankish King of Cologne, living 420, kinsman of Clovis I.
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: !The greatest of all the Franks was Clovis, the King of the Franks.  Clovis made his headquarters in Paris and from there directed the conquests which  made him master of Gaul.  Clothilda, his wife was a Christian.  Thr
2 CONC ough her influence Clovis was baptized in theh city of Reims.  Thus their ruler had accepted the new faith, the people of Gaul  became Christians
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-7369
1 NOTE AFN:9GBJ-ZH
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: Semi-legendary King of the Salian Franks and father of Merovech, founder of the Merovingian Dynasty. Called ", the Long Hair" or ", the Hairy" because of the length of his hair. From then on the Merovingians were called
2 CONC  the "Long Haired Kings" and the cutting of a king's hair represented his loss of royal power. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to legend his father was Pharamond (r.409-426), the first King of the Salian Franks after the departure of the Romans from Gaul. In history, Clodio was probably real. He lived in Thuringian territory, and ruled at the sa
2 CONC me time as the semi-legendary kings Theudemer and Richemer. All that is known of his reign is that he took the town of Cambrai from the Romans. He was succeeded by his semi-legendary son Merovech. (Unlike Merovech and Clodio, Chil
2 CONC deric I, Merovech's son, was very real and cannot be considered fictional.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT  http://www.ghgcorp.com/shetler/oldimp/016.html
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT Bu86 http://www.gendex.com/users/Enf_Bry/i2709.html#I15512
2 CONT http://www.art-science.com/Ken/Genealogy/PD/ch46_Clovis.html
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT http://www.art-science.com/Ken/Genealogy/PD/ch46_Clovis.html
1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT Riparian Frankish king
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
1 NOTE Ruled France 428-447
2 CONT
2 CONT KINGS OF THE FRANKS
2 CONT
2 CONT CLODIO / CLODIAN VI (AD 426 - 447/8), King of the Salian Franks(Cambrai). According to legend his father was Pharamond (409 - 426), thefirst king of the Salian Franks after the departure of the Romans fromGaul. His son Merovech (s
2 CONC ucceeding King of the Salian Franks), was thefounder of the Merovingian Dynasty. Called "the Long Hair" or "the Hairy"because of the length of his hair. From then on the Merovingians werecalled the "Long Haired Kings" and the cutt
2 CONC ing of a king's hairrepresented his loss of royal power.
2 CONT
2 CONT In history, Clodio was probably real. He lived in Thuringian territory,and ruled at the same time as the semi-legendary kings Theudemer andRichemer. All that is known of his reign is that he took the town ofCambrai from the Romans
2 CONC . He was succeeded by his semi-legendary sonMerovech. Although Merovech and Clodio are considered to besemi-legendary, Merovech's son, Childeric I, was very real and cannot beconsidered fictional.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:http://homepages.tesco.net/~plk33/plk33/History/FeaturesEurope/FranceKings.htm
1 NOTE AFN:9GBJ-ZH
1 NOTE Hij is ook bekend onder diverse varianten als Clodio, Cloio, Chlogio; was. '''Zijn vader zou Pharamond zijn''', die naam komt echter alleen voor in bronnen van geruime tijd na zijn dood, en is daarom mogelijk niet historisch.
2 CONT Er wordt vermoed dat hij oorspronkelijk uit Thuringen kwam - zijn machtsbasis was Dispargum in terminum Thuringorum (Dispargum aan de grens van Thuringen); er is echter ook een theorie dat 'Thuringorum' een schrijffout voor 'Tungr
2 CONC orum' (Tongeren) is.
2 CONT Rond 448 wordt hij verslagen nabij Artesië; desondanks wordt vermoed dat hij regeerde over het gebied van het huidige België tot aan de Somme. Hij werd opgevolgd door Merovech, '''vermoedelijk''' zijn zoon.
1 NOTE Also known as Critinus.
1 NOTE Alias/AKA Chlodio, Clodion Famundson             Sigambrisk høvding
