2 CONC 52321?through=6000000011540372224 BERTHECHAR] [Bertaire] King of the Thuringians & his wife --- (Erfurt 518-Poitiers 13 Aug 587, bur Poitiers, basilique Sainte-Marie-hors-les-Murs).  Gregory of Tours names Radegund as the orphaned
2 CONC  daughter of Berthar[154].  The Vitæ Sanctæ Radegundis names "Radegundis natione barbare de regione Thoringa" and her "avo rege Bessino, patruo Hermenfredo, patre rege Bertechario"[155].  In a later passage, Gregory records that, 
2 CONC after the Frankish invasion of Thuringia, Radegund formed part of the booty taken home by Clotaire I King of the Franks, who later married her[156].  The testament of Radegund dated to [584/87] survives[157].  Gregory of Tours rec
2 CONC ords the death of St Radegund on 13 Aug[158].  She was canonised, her feast day is 13 Aug[159].''' 
