2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy Medlands page on Vandals, Suevi, and Visigoths (covering her second marriage):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/VANDALS,%20SUEVI,%20VISIGOTHS.htm#Hunericdied484
2 CONT
2 CONT HUNERIC (-484).  
2 CONT *The Victoris Vitensis Historia names "Huniricus maior filius [Geiserici]" when recording that he succeeded on the death of his father[27].  
2 CONT *He lived as a hostage at Ravenna in 442[28].  
2 CONT *He succeeded his father in 477 as HUNERIC King of the Vandals in Africa.  The Victoris Tonnennensis Epsicopi Chronicon records that "Hugnericus filius eius" succeeded his father in 464 and reigned for 7 years and 5 months[29].  T
2 CONC he Victoris Vitensis Historia names him "rex Hunirix Wandalorum et Alanorum" when recording his exploits in Africa[30].  
2 CONT *m firstly ([429] or after[31], repudiated 442) --- the Visigoth, daughter of THEODERIC I King of the Visigoths & his wife ---.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  She was se
2 CONC nt back to her father at the time of the 442 revolt with her nose and ears mutilated[32].  
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly ([455]) as her second husband, EUDOXIA, widow of PALADIUS, daughter of Emperor VALENTINIAN III, Emperor in the West & his wife Eudoxia.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicon of Bishop Idatius records that Maximus arranged the marriage of “filio suo ex priore coniuge Palladio” and “Valentiniani filiam” in 455[33].  After the death of her father, his successor forced Eudoxia to marry his s
2 CONC on, but she was captured by Genseric King of the Vandals during his attack on Rome and taken back to north Africa with her mother and sister[34].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Procopius names "Eudocia and Placidia" as children of "Eudoxia…and Valentinian", recording that Eudoxia was married to Huneric, the older son of Gaiseric, while the other daughter was the wife of Olybrius, a Roman senator[35].  Th
2 CONC e Chronicon of Bishop Idatius records that one daughter of Valentinian married “Gentoni Gaiserici filio” and the other “Olybrio Senatori Urbis Romæ”[36].  The Victoris Tonnennensis Epsicopi Chronicon records that "Hugnericus" marr
2 CONC ied "Valentiniani filiam" who had been abducted from Rome in captivity[37].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Huneric & his second wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT a)  HILDERIC ([480]-murdered 534). 
2 CONT * Iordanes names "Ilderich" as fifth Vandal king in Africa but does not specify his relationship to Thrasamund, his predecessor[38].  The Victoris Tonnennensis Epsicopi Chronicon records the succession in 523 of "Hilderix, qui ex 
2 CONC Valentiniani imperatoris filia…et Ugnerico iuncta natus est" and that he reigned for 7 years and 3 months[39].  He succeeded [his presumed cousin] in 523 as HILDERIC King of the Vandals in Africa 523.  
2 CONT *He broke the Vandal alliance with Theodoric King of Italy, supporting the emperor at Constantinople instead[40].  
2 CONT *He was deposed by his cousin Gailamir in 530.  Iordanes records that Hilderic was deposed by "Gelimer" but does not specify the relationship between the two[41].  
2 CONT *The Victoris Tonnennensis Epsicopi Chronicon records that Hilderic was deposed by "Gerlimer" in 531, imprisoned with his sons, and killed in 534 "cum quibusdam generis eius affinibus"[42].  
2 CONT *m ---.  The name of Hilderic's wife is not known.  Hilderic & his wife had --- children.
2 CONT
