3 NOTE Hamdir, Sörli, and Erpr were three brothers in Norse mythology who have a historic basis in the history of the Goths.
4 CONT
4 CONT Legend
4 CONT According to the Edda and Völsunga saga, Hamdir and Sörli were the sons of Gjuki's daughter Guðrún and King Jonakr. Erpr was the son of Jonakr from an earlier marriage. Svanhildr, the daughter of Sigurðr and Guðrún, was also raise
4 CONC d by Jonakr.
4 CONT
4 CONT King Jörmunrekr (Ermanaric) proposed to Svanhildr through his son Randver, but the treacherous Bicke said that Randver tried to win Svanhild's love. Consequently, Jörmunrekr sentenced Randver to death by hanging and had Svanhildr 
4 CONC trampled to death by horses. Guðrún then agitated her sons Hamdir and Sörli to avenge their half-sister. When Sörli and Hamdir met Erpr en route, they did not understand his riddles and, thinking him arrogant, killed him.
4 CONT
4 CONT During the night, they arrived and they cut off Jörmunrek's hands and feet. This made Jörmunrekr wake up and he cried for his housecarls. Hamdir said that if Erpr had been alive he would have cut off the head. The housecarls could
4 CONC  not kill the two brothers with sharp weapons, but an old one-eyed man (Odin) advised them to kill them with stones.
4 CONT
4 CONT This is why skaldic poetry used the "sorrow of Jonakr's sons" as a kenning for stones.
