1 OCCU Queen of The Franks, Reine, Brunhild, queen of the Frankish kingdom known as Austrasia (in present-day northeastern France and southwestern Germany), , Princesa de los Visigodos
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''BRUNECHILDIS''' [Brunequilda/Brunechilde] of the Visigoths, daughter of ATANAGILDO King of the Visigoths & his wife Gosvinta --- ([545/50]-Renève-sur-Vingeanne Autumn 613, bur Autun, abbaye de Saint-Martin).
2 CONT
2 CONT x  (early 566) as her first husband SIGEBERT ([535]-murdered Vitry [Nov/Dec] 575, bur Lambres transferred to Soissons Saint-Médard)
2 CONT s/o CLOTAIRE I [Chlothachar] King of the Franks & his third wife Ingundis [Ingonde] 
2 CONT * INGUNDIS [Ingonde] ([567/68]-[in Africa or Sicily] Autumn 586) x (579) HERMENEGILDO of the Visigoths, son of LEOVIGILDO King of the Visigoths & his first wife --- (-murdered Tarragona 13 Apr 586). 
2 CONT *CHILDEBERT II King of the Franks. (570-[2/28] Mar 596) x m FAILEUBA
2 CONT *CHLODESINDIS [Clodesinde] ([575/76]-after 594)
2 CONT *NN daughter x (before 609) CHRODOALD, Duke [of Bavaria] [Agilolfinger]
2 CONT
