1 OCCU 8th King of the Ostrogoths (378-409)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''VALARAVANS'''
2 CONT s/o VULTWULF
2 CONT *VINITHARIUS 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HUNGARY.htm#_Toc146273201
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Hungary:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HUNGARY.htm#Theodemirdied474A
2 CONT
2 CONT VULTWULF (Ostrogoth Generation 10)
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Ansila et Ediulf, Vultuulf et Hermenerig" as the sons of Achiulf[35].
2 CONT
2 CONT VALARAVANS (Ostrogoth Generation 11)
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Valaravans" as the son of Vultwulf[36]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VINITHARIUS (Ostrogoth Generation 12)
2 CONT
2 CONT Iordanes names "Vinitharius" as the son of Valaravans[37]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT [35] Iordanes Getarum, MGH Auct. ant. V.1, p. 77. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [36] Iordanes Getarum, MGH Auct. ant. V.1, p. 77. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [37] Iordanes Getarum, MGH Auct. ant. V.1, p. 77. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Jordanes' Getica (Iordanes' Getarum):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://people.ucalgary.ca/~vandersp/Courses/texts/jordgeti.html#visi
2 CONT
2 CONT XIV 
2 CONT
2 CONT (79) Now the first of these heroes, as they themselves relate in their legends, was Gapt, who begat Hulmul. And Hulmul begat Augis; and Augis begat him who was called Amal, from whom the name of the Amali comes. This Amal begat Hi
2 CONC sarnis. Hisarnis moreover begat Ostrogotha, and Ostrogotha begat Hunuil, and Hunuil likewise begat Athal. Athal begat Achiulf and Oduulf. Now Achiulf begat Ansila and Ediulf, Vultuulf and Hermanaric. And Vultuulf begat Valaravans 
2 CONC and Valaravans begat Vinitharius. Vinitharius moreover begat Vandalarius; 
2 CONT
2 CONT (80) Vandalarius begat Thiudimer and Valamir and Vidimer; and Thiudimer begat Theodoric. Theodoric begat Amalasuentha; Amalasuentha bore Athalaric and Mathesuentha to her husband Eutharic, whose race was thus joined to hers in kin
2 CONC ship. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (81) For the aforesaid Hermanaric, the son of Achiulf, begat Hunimund, and Hunimund begat Thorismud. Now Thorismud begat Beremud, Beremud begat Veteric, and Veteric likewise begat Eutharic, who married Amalasuentha and begat Athal
2 CONC aric and Mathesuentha. Athalaric died in the years of his childhood, and Mathesuentha married Vitiges, to whom she bore no child. Both of them were taken together by Belisarius to Constantinople. When Vitiges passed from human aff
2 CONC airs, Germanus the patrician, a cousin of the Emperor Justinian, took Mathesuentha in marriage and made her a Patrician Ordinary. And of her he begat a son, also called Germanus. But upon the death of Germanus, she determined to r
2 CONC emain a widow. Now how and in what wise the kingdom of the Amali was overthrown we shall keep to tell in its proper place, if the Lord help us.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From German Wikipedia (still looking for other sources to back this assertion up):
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelige
2 CONT
2 CONT Amalaberga (* um 385 oder 400, † 443), Tochter von Walderavans (auch: Valeravans, Walaranvans) von Ostrogothien (vgl. Goten), verheiratet mit Wedelphe (auch: Wildelphe von Sachsen), Mutter von Basine (auch: Basina) von Sachsen; ve
2 CONC rheiratet mit dem Ost- und Westgotenkönig Theoderich (auch: Theoderid I), Mutter von Eurich I. und dem Ostgotenkönig Theoderich der Große
2 CONT
2 CONT (In English - Amalaberga (c.385 or 400, d. 443), daughter of Walderavans (also: Valeravans, Walaranvans) of the Ostrogoths (Goths), married with Wedelphe (also Wildelphe of the Saxons), mother of Basine (also Basina) of the Saxons
2 CONC ; marrried with Visigoth king Theodorich (also Theoderid I), mother of Eurich I and the Ostrogoth King Theodoric the Great.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wedelphe (auch: Wildelphe II.) von Sachsen; * um 410), verheiratet mit Chlodwig (auch: Ludwig) von Köln
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Literatur
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerhard Köbler: Gotisches Wörterbuch. Brill, Leiden 1989, ISBN 90-04-09128-9
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel summary:
2 CONT
2 CONT From Jordanes, Valaravans is established as a son of Vultwulf, who was brother of King Airmanareiks (Hermenrich) of the Goths. Valaravans would have likely faded into obscurity but for the rebellion of his son Vinitharius "The Jus
2 CONC t", a warlord who killed off the leadership of the Antes and prompted a response from Hun Emperor Bulümar "Sheke," or "Balamber". Vinitharius' death marked the end of Ostrogoth resistance to the Huns.
2 CONT
2 CONT Valaravans is said by Gerhard Kobler to have fathered not only Vinitharius, but a woman named Almaberga, supposedly the first woman by that name, who married a Saxon king named Widelphe. Widelphe is supposed to have been the fathe
2 CONC r of "Basina", the wife of Thuringian King Basin who ran of with Childeric of the Franks after the latter was taken in as a refugee for 8 years. No other source supports this assertion (certainly it is not published in FMG's Medla
2 CONC nds). Verification of Kobler's source for this would be welcome.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT B: 323, 330, 335
2 CONT --------------------
