2 CONT [edit]Religious policy
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Wein, Yazdegerd I was a wise, benevolent, and astute ruler.[8] He was also known for his religious tolerance, towards both Christians and Jews. For example, the Talmud (Ksubos, 61a) relates that Ameimar, Rav Ashi, and
2 CONC  Mar Zutra would sit in his court. However, excessive zeal of the Christian bishop of Ctesiphon, Abdaas, provoked a reaction, and when he tried to burn the Great Fire temple of Ctesiphon, Yazdegerd I turned against the Christians 
2 CONC (see following).
