1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dabuya '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dabuya''' or '''Dabuyih''' (Persian: دابویه‎), was the Dabuyid ruler (ispahbadh) of Tabaristan. He succeeded his father Gil Gavbara in 660 and reigned until his death in 712. His son, Farrukhan the Great succeeded him.
2 CONT
