1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT Theodosius II, imperator was a gentle, scholarly, easily dominated man who
2 CONT allowed his government to be run by a succession of relatives and ministers.
2 CONT He was made coemperor by his father in 402.1 He succeeded his father as
2 CONT Eastern Emperor in 408.1 He governed by Anthemius, praetorian prefect of the
2 CONT East, who was his first regent between 408 and 414.1 Emperor in Eastern Roman
2 CONT Empire, between 408 and 28 July 450.4,2 He publically reprimanded the Jewish
2 CONT Patriarch Gamaliel II and stripped him of the rank of 'praefectus praetorio'
2 CONT in 415.5 He married Empress Aelia Eudokia of Athens, daughter of Leontios of
2 CONT Athens, on 7 June 421; The marriage was arrainged by Theodosius' sister,
2 CONT Plechtrude.3,6 He abolished the Jewish Patriarchate and diverted the Jewish
2 CONT tax to the imperial treasury in 429.5 He published the Theodosian Code which,
2 CONT among others, imposed the death penalty on any Jew who tries to convert a
2 CONT Christian to Judaism in 439.
1 NOTE AUGUSTUS 402; EMPORER OF THE EAST 408-450
1 NOTE Known for the Codex Theodosius and the great walls of Constantinople. Pulcheria made him favor the eastern branch of christianity. She was also anti semetic and that negative view caused the destruction of synogogues. Theodosius o
2 CONC rdered the execution of Gamaliel VI, the Nasi of the Jewish Sanhedrin in 435 for authorizing the building of new synogogues.
1 NOTE Teodósio II , imperador do Oriente de 408 a 450. Nasceu em Constantinopla em 401 e morreu em 450. Também é cognominado por «Moço» por ter iniciado o seu reinado com apenas 7 anos.
2 CONT De fraco carácter, deixou-se influenciar por aqueles que o rodeavam, nomeadamente a sua irmã e a sua esposa. Desenvolveu uma política externa pouco brilhante e deixou os monofisitas triunfarem no concílio de Éfeso (431).
2 CONT Após o papa Celestino I ter excomungado, em 430, Nestório, o patriarca de Constantinopla cujas teses foram derrotadas no Concílio de Éfeso, Teodósio ordenou que toda a vasta obra do patricarca fosse queimada.
2 CONT O seu reinado foi marcado pelo alargamento das fronteiras do Império (apesar de algumas derrotas pesadas, como contra as forças hunas de Átila) e pela controvérsia religiosa. Mandou redigir o Código Teodosiano.
