1 NOTE The man who became General Constantius of the Roman Empire, was born about 380 in Illyria (on the East Adriatic coast of the Balkan peninsula.)
2 CONT
2 CONT General Constantius had been made Augustus, Emperor of the Roman Empire by his brother-in-law Honorius in 421, but Emperor Constantius III died seven months later.  Leaving his widow Galla Placidia, and their young son, Valentinia
2 CONC n as his heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT General Constantius defeated the ursurper Constantine in 411.
