1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT Roman Emperor; came from Naissus (modern Nis, Yugos.) in the province of
2 CONT Moesia.1 He was one of the most important magistri militum of Honorius after
2 CONT the death of Stilicho in 408.2 He helped the western Roman emperor Flavius
2 CONT Honorius, overthrow the usurping emperor Constantine (Flavius Claudius
2 CONT Constantinus) in 411 in Arelate (Arles), (France).1 Magister militum ("master
2 CONT of the soldiers") in 411.  He and Galla Placidia the elder, augusta became
2 CONT involved -- on the losing side -- in the controversy over the election of a
2 CONT new bishop of Rome in 419. He was Catholic. He was so described: a fierce
2 CONT warrior in public, but he was far more relaxed in private and at banquets.2 He
2 CONT married the sister of the Western Emperor Honorius, and served as co-Emperor
2 CONT with him for 7 months until his death in 421. He was appointed coemperor of
2 CONT the West by Honorius, with the title augustus, on 8 February 421.1 Augustus in
2 CONT Western Roman Empire, between 8 February 421 and 2 September 421.
