2 CONT King of the Vandals; The marriage of the Western Emperor Valentinian III's
2 CONT daughter to the son of the brilliant Vandal king Gaiseric, Huneric, was a
2 CONT carefully thought-out political manoeuver. "Gaiseric came suddenly to Rome
2 CONT with his forces and captured the city... He even led away as captives
2 CONT surviving senators, along with their wives; along with them he also carried
2 CONT off to Carthage in Africa the empress Eudoxia, who had summoned him, her
2 CONT daughter Placidia, the wife of the patrician Olybrius, who then was staying at
2 CONT Constantinople, and even the maiden Eudocia. After he had returned, Gaiseric
2 CONT gave the younger Eudocia, a maiden, the daughter of the empress Eudoxia, to
2 CONT his son Huneric in marriage, and he held them both, the mother and the
2 CONT daughter, in great honor" (Chron. 366). He married Princess of the Visigoths
2 CONT N. N. Balthi, daughter of Theodoric I, rex Gotthorum and N. N. the Visigoth,
2 CONT in 429.1,3 He was born after 440 in Maghrib. He was the son of Gaiseric, King
2 CONT of the Vandals.4,5 He married Eudokia "the Younger", daughter of Flavius
2 CONT Placidus Valentinianus, imperator and Licinia Eudokia Theodosia, augusta, in
2 CONT 455; His 2nd.6,7,5  King of the Vandals in Maghrib, North Africa, between 477
2 CONT and 484.
1 NOTE King of Vandals Born in Cathage. Geiseric's son.
2 CONT The usurper, Gelimer took the throne by force and imprisoned Huneric. he didn't kill him until
2 CONT Justinian, an ally of Huneric declared war on Gelimer. It was a decision made as an excuse to regain Africa from the Vandals. As a result of this war, Gelimer ordered Huneric's murder.
