1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Atanagildo-I-rey-de-los-visigodos/6000000025181544721
2 CONT * Disputed as husband of https://www.geni.com/people/Flavia-Juliana/6000000003975586314?through=6000000003040988215
2 CONT * Speculative father of [http://www.geni.com/people/Ardabasto/6000000012136748824 Ardabasto].
2 CONT * Not a known king of the Visigoths 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The photo is of Athanagild I not subject of this profile. Athanagild II, purportedly son the Hermenegild and Ingund was taken to Constantinople on the death of his father, raised there by Emperor Mauricius and subsequently married
2 CONC  his niece, Flavia Juliana.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Cawley’s Project Medieval Lands.  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/VANDALS,%20SUEVI,%20VISIGOTHS.htm#_Toc359944956 '''SPAIN: VANDALS, SUEVI & VISIGOTHS''']  v4.0 Updated 28 February 2019 “Chapter 3.    VISIGOTHS in SPAIN 5
2 CONC 31-711.”
2 CONT
2 CONT King Leovigildo & his first wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         HERMENEGILDO “the Holy” ([550/55]-murdered Tarragona 13 Apr 586). … The Iohannis Abbatis Biclarensis Chronica records that Hermenegildo was sent into exile in 584 and in 585 was killed "in urbe Tarraconensi" by "Sisbert
2 CONC o"[224].  He was canonised in 1586. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (579) INGUNDIS [Ingonde] of the Franks, daughter of SIGEBERT I King of the Franks & his wife Brunechildis of the Visigoths ([567/68]-in Africa Autumn 586).  ...  She fled to Africa with her son after her husband was killed, seek
2 CONC ing refuge with the Eastern Emperor[229].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Hermenegildo and his wife had one child:
2 CONT * a)         son .  Paulus Diaconus records that, after Ingundis was captured following her husband's death, "filius eius" was handed over to Emperor Mauricius and taken to Constantinople[230].  same person as…?  ATANAGILDO.  Sala
2 CONC zar y Castro, in his genealogical table of the Visigothic kings, shows "'''Atanagildo'''" as the son of Hermenegildo, as well as his marriage to "Flavia Juliana hija de Pedro Augusto, hermano del Emperador Mauricio", and their son
2 CONC s "Paulo" and "Ardavasto", as well as the latter´s marriage to "prima, hija o hermana del Rey Cindasuindo"[231] (see below).  The primary sources on which these statements are based are not specified.  The table includes numerous 
2 CONC errors and the information should therefore be viewed with caution. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingund_(wife_of_Hermenegild)
2 CONT
2 CONT 17th-century Spanish genealogist Luis Bartolomé de Salazar y Castro gave Ardabast's father as Athanagild, the son of Saint Hermenegild and Ingund, and his mother as Flavia Juliana, a daughter of Peter Augustus and niece of the Emp
2 CONC eror Maurice.[20] This imperial connection is disputed by Christian Settipani, who says that the only source for Athanagild's marriage to Flavia Julia is José Pellicer, who he claims to be a forger.[21]
2 CONT
2 CONT * 20.  Luis de Salazar y Castro, Historia Genealógica de la Casa de Lara (Madrid, 1696) vol. I, p. 45. < [https://archive.org/stream/bub_gb_AffI0i1mO5wC#page/n64/mode/1up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT * 21.  Christian Settipani, Les ancêtres de Charlemagne, p. 431.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermenegildo
2 CONT
2 CONT >According to traditional genealogy, from his marriage to the Frankish princess Ingunda was born Prince Atanagildo, who in turn married Flavia Juliana, paternal niece of the Byzantine emperor Mauricio, the latter would be the pare
2 CONC nts of Paulo Ardabasto, whose son of the Goth king Ervigio. Based on this genealogy, the kings of Asturias and León (Astur-Leonese d'adinasia), the kings of Pamplona and the first kings of Aragon were considered, as well as the co
2 CONC unts of Castile, descendants of San Hermenegildo.7 However, this genealogy has been discussed.
2 CONT
2 CONT
