1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT King of Kent 560-616; Sainted
2 CONT ’thelberht became king of Kent when his father King Ermenric died in 560, and
2 CONT he also exercised sway over Essex where his nephew Sabert was king. In 568,
2 CONT ’thelberht attempted a westward expansion in Wessex, where he was defeated by
2 CONT King Ceawlin at Wibbandune. In 597, Saint Augustine landed in Kent, and while
2 CONT at first ’thelberht was tolerant of Christianity he was baptized himself (the
2 CONT first British king ever) but did not force the conversion of his subjects. In
2 CONT 604, he founded the see of Rochester (given to Bishop Jestus), and he is known
2 CONT to have compiled a code of laws that was the first of its kind in Britian.
1 NOTE He ruled from 565 to 616. He brought Christianity to Kent, extablishing Canterbury as a Bishopric.
