1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nothing is known specifically about the wife of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Edeko-Chief-of-the-Scirii/6000000015965884288 Edeko]''' and mother of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Odoacer-1st-Germanic-King-of-Italy
2 CONC /6000000004257979021 Odoacer]'''. The question is a matter of academic interest because it bears on Odoacer's ethnicity. There are late genealogical claims that she was an Herule; an Ostrogoth; the daughter of '''[http://www.geni.
2 CONC com/people/Hunimund-King-of-the-Suevi/6000000008019616465 Hunimund]''', king of the Swabians; etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a reconstruction by Stephan Krautschick, Odoacer and '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Onoulphus/6000000014132319403 Onoulphus]''' were brothers of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Flavius-Armatus/6000000000316459716 Flavi
2 CONC us Armatus]''', so they were also nephews of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Flavius-Basiliscus-Augustus/6000000007167194211 Basiliscus]''' and '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Aelia-Verina/6000000007166533573 Empress Verina]'''. The
2 CONC refore, Edeko's wife must have been a sister of Verina.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Krautschick, Stephan (1986). "Zwei Aspekte des Jahres 476". Historia 35: pp. 344–371.
