2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Arcadius (377/378–1 May 408) was Byzantine Emperor in the Eastern half of the Roman Empire from 395 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reign January 383 - 395 (Augustus under his father);
2 CONT
2 CONT 395 - 1 May 408 (emperor in the east, with his brother Honorius emperor in the west)
2 CONT
