2 CONT Biography:  Roman Emperor (395-408) who ruled the eastern half of the Roman Empire. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Arcadius, eldest son of Theodosius I and Flacilla, ruled the eastern half of the Roman Empire while his brother Honorius ruled the western half. Although the brothers co-ruled, Arcadius was under the control of Rufinus and Honoriu
2 CONC s was under the control of Flavius Stilicho, whose desire to control both emperors was so great he assassinated Rufinus in 395. The plan backfired and Arcadius' advisor filled the void. In 399, although he was successful in quelli
2 CONC ng a revolt of the Gothic officials and mercenaries in Constantinople, he was considered a weakened ruler who was dominated by his wife Eudoxia. John Chrysostom, the Patriarch of Constantinople, strongly disliked Eudoxia and knowi
2 CONC ng such, she used her connections to have him deposed in 404. After her death, Arcadius was dominated the remainder of his rule by Anthemius the Praetorian Prefect who made peace with Stilicho in the West. He died in 408 only nomi
2 CONC nally in control of his empire.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Contributor: Kimberly J. Largent 
