2 CONT ALARIC (-Bruttium, southern Italy end 410).  First mentioned in 391 when he moved southwards into Greece, he suffered several military setbacks but succeeded in resettling the Goths in Macedonia[18].  He was elected in 395 as ALAR
2 CONC IC King of the Visigoths.  He entered the western part of the Roman Empire in 401, and by the end of the year had attacked Venetia and was threatening Milan.  Alaric was defeated by the Romans in 402 at Pollenza, and in 403 at Ver
2 CONC ona, after which the Goths abandoned Italy and settled in Dalmatia and Pannonia[19].  King Alaric returned to Italy in 408, the Goths' attacks culminating in the sack of Rome in Aug 410[20].  Procopius records that Alaric died fro
2 CONC m illness[21].  m ---.  The name(s) of King Alaric's wife or wives is not known.  King Alaric had children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         daughter.  [22]m THEODERIC (-killed in battle near Troyes 451).  He was elected to succeed in 418 on the death of King Walia as THEODERIC I King of the Visigoths. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         other children.
