1 NOTE KING OF THE VANDALS AT CARTHAGE 439-477; NAME MEANS "WHIP-KING"; TOOK CARTHAGE
2 CONT IN 439
1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT "The Rod of God" King of the Vandals in Spain 419-428; at Carthage 439-477
2 CONT King of the Vandals in Spain, between 419 and 428. He succeeded his brother
2 CONT Gunderic in 426 in Baetica (modern Andalusia), Spain.2 King of the Alans
2 CONT between 428 and 477.2 He was orchestrated a mass move of his people, purported
2 CONT to number some 80,000, to Maghrib (North Africa) in May 428. Evidently he was
2 CONT invited to Africa by the governor, Count Bonifacius, who wished to use the
2 CONT military strength of the Vandals in his struggle against the imperial
2 CONT government.1 He was advanced eastwards in Maghrib and took Hippo Regius in
2 CONT 430. They took the city after a long siege during which St. Augustine died.1
2 CONT He was turned on Count Bonifacius, and defeated him, in 430 in Maghrib. He
2 CONT then crushed the joint forces of the Eastern and Western empires that had been
2 CONT sent against him.1 He was concluded an agreement with Rome that the Vandal
2 CONT state in Africa became a Federate of Rome in 435.1 King of the Vandals in
2 CONT Maghrib, between 439 and 477. He overthrew Roman overlordship and seized the
2 CONT important mediterranean city of Carthage, allowing him to create an
2 CONT independent autocracy, a second power in the mediterranean alongside Rome, on
2 CONT 19 October 439 in Maghrib.2 He was concluded a treaty with Rome in 442.
2 CONT Therein the Vandals were recognized as masters of proconsular Africa,
2 CONT Byzacena, and part of Numidia. Gaiseric was perhaps the most perceptive
2 CONT barbarian king of the 5th century in realizing the total weakness of the
2 CONT empire. Gaiseric's fleet soon came to control much of the western
2 CONT Mediterranean, and he annexed the Balearic Islands, Sardinia, Corsica, and
2 CONT Sicily.1 He sacked Rome in June 455 in Italy.1 He defeated the first major
2 CONT Roman effort, led by the Emperor Majorian, to remove him in 460.1 He defeated
2 CONT the second attempt of Rome, led by Basiliscus, to oust him in 468.
1 NOTE a conquis la province Romaine d'Afrique du Nord et Fondateur du Royaume des Vandales en 429 
2 CONT Prend Carthage en 439, saccage Rome en 455 et retourne à Carthage avec l'Imperatrice Licinia Eudoxia et ses deux filles en otage. Son fils Huneric épousera Eudocia la fille d'Eudoxia.
1 NOTE Genserico (c. 389 – 25 de janeiro de 477), rei dos vândalos e alanos entre 428 e 477. Foi peçaa chave nos conflitos travados no século V pelo Império Romano do Ocidente, e durante os seus quase cinquenta anos de reinado elevou uma
2 CONC  tribo germânica relativamente insignificante à categoria de potência mediterrânea.
2 CONT Filho ilegítimo do rei vândalo Godegisilo, supõe-se que nasceu nas inmediações do lago Balatão por volta de 389. Foi escolhido rei em 428 com a morte do seu meio irmão Gunderico. Brilhante e muito versado na arte militar, buscou o
2 CONC  modo de aumentar o poder e a prosperidade do seu povo, que residia na época na Hispania Bética e que havia sofrido os ataques dos mais numerosos visigodos. Assim, pouco depois de ascender ao trono, Genserico decidiu ceder a Hispa
2 CONC nia aos seus rivais, empregando para isso a poderosa frota criada no reinado do seu predecessor.
