2 CONT XIV 
2 CONT
2 CONT (79) Now the first of these heroes, as they themselves relate in their legends, was Gapt, who begat Hulmul. And Hulmul begat Augis; and Augis begat him who was called Amal, from whom the name of the Amali comes. This Amal begat Hi
2 CONC sarnis. Hisarnis moreover begat Ostrogotha, and Ostrogotha begat Hunuil, and Hunuil likewise begat Athal. Athal begat Achiulf and Oduulf. Now Achiulf begat Ansila and Ediulf, Vultuulf and Hermanaric. And Vultuulf begat Valaravans 
2 CONC and Valaravans begat Vinitharius. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel summary: Odwulf or Oduulf is mentioned mostly by those quoting or sourcing Jordanes' Getica (which doesn't say a whole lot on his life) or in reference to the English baby name of Odwulf meaning "Wealthy Wolf".  Some 
2 CONC online family trees misrepresent him as a Gothic (or Ostrogothic) King. During his period, according to Jordanes, the succession of Gothic kings were known to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Ariaric and Aoric
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Geberich
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Airmanareiks
2 CONT
2 CONT Other historic Gothic leaders that appear at the head of raiding or invading parties during his period include:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Criiva (leader of the 251 AD invasion)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Cannabaudes (leader of the 271 AD invasion)
2 CONT
2 CONT Odwulf was merely a member of the Amal family.
