2 CONC ld until her untimely death in her early thirties in 642. This death allowed him to fall under the influence of the secular magnates, who reduced the royal power in their own favour.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clovis' wife, Balthild, was an Anglo-Saxon aristocrat sold into slavery in Gaul. She had been owned by Clovis' mayor of the palace, Ebroin, who gave her to him to garner royal favour. She bore him three sons who all became kings a
2 CONC fter his death. The eldest, Chlothar, succeeded him and his second eldest, Childeric, was eventually placed on the Austrasian throne by Ebroin. The youngest, Theuderic, succeeded Childeric in Neustria and eventually became the sol
2 CONC e king of the Franks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clovis was a minor for almost the whole of his reign. He is sometimes regarded as king of Austrasia during the interval 656-657 when Childebert the Adopted had usurped the throne. He is often regarded as an early roi fainéant.
