1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Flavius Armatus''' (died 477) was a Byzantine military commander, magister militum under Emperors '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Leo-I-Roman-Emperor/6000000007159259859 Leo I]''', '''[http://www.geni.com/people/
2 CONC Flavius-Basiliscus-Augustus/6000000007167194211 Basiliscus]''' and '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Zeno-Eastern-Roman-Emperor/6000000002106208023 Zeno]''', and consul. He was instrumental in the rebellion of Basiliscus against Zeno
2 CONC , and in his subsequent fall. Armatus was killed by order of Zeno. The murderer was Armatus' friend '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Onoulphus/6000000014132319403 Onoulphus]'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Armatus was a nephew of Basiliscus and of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Aelia-Verina/6000000007166533573 Empress Verina]''', the wife of Leo I. It is known that Armatus had a son, also named '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Basilis
2 CONC cus-Caesar/6000000000316339843 Basiliscus]'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a reconstruction by Stephan Krautschick, Armatus was a brother of Onoulphus and '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Odoacer-1st-Germanic-King-of-Italy/6000000004257979021 Odoacer]''', who were also then nephews of Basilisc
2 CONC us and Verina. Therefore, Amatus' father must have been '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Edeko-Chief-of-the-Scirii/6000000015965884288 Edeko]''', the father of Onoulphus and Odoacer. In particular, this interpretation sheds light on
2 CONC  why Armatus was so keen to help Onoulphus, and that it was his own brother that killed him.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Krautschick, Stephan (1986). "Zwei Aspekte des Jahres 476". Historia 35: pp. 344–371.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armatus English]
