1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Onoulphus''', also '''Onoulf''', '''Unulf''' and '''Hunulf''' (died 493) was a general of Scirian origin in the late fifth century. He served as ''magister militum per Illyricum'' from 477 to 479 as a general of
2 CONC  the Eastern Roman Empire, then afterwards was a general for his brother '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Odoacer-1st-Germanic-King-of-Italy/6000000004257979021 Odoacer]''', king of Italy, until their death.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the traditional story, Onoulphus was a poor barbarian, befriended by '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Flavius-Armatus/6000000000316459716 Flavius Armatus]''', then made comes, then commander of Illyricum. However, Onoul
2 CONC phus killed his friend Armatus in 477 on the order of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Zeno-Eastern-Roman-Emperor/6000000002106208023 Emperor Zeno]'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a reconstruction by Stephan Krautschick, Onoulphus was a brother of Armatus, so Onoulphus was also a nephew of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Flavius-Basiliscus-Augustus/6000000007167194211 Basiliscus]''' and '''[http
2 CONC ://www.geni.com/people/Aelia-Verina/6000000007166533573 Empress Verina]'''. In particular, this interpretation sheds light on why Armatus was so keen to help Onoulphus, and that it was his own brother that killed him
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Krautschick, Stephan (1986). "Zwei Aspekte des Jahres 476". Historia 35: pp. 344–371.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Onoulphus English]
