1 NOTE RULED WESTERN ROMAN EMPIRE 375-392
1 NOTE After Maximus was defeated Theodosius installed Valentinian's court at Vienne in Gaul. Theodosius installed a Frankish general, Arbogast as Magister Militum for the western provinces. Acting in the name of Valentinian but actually
2 CONC  serving Theodosius. Valentinian disliked being under the authority of one of his generals. But the stage had been set long ago that Roman emperors becoming figureheads of government when actually it was their generals who ran the
2 CONC ir country. Valentinian made the grave mistake of dismissing Arbogast. The general ignored the order. Ot didn't end there.
2 CONT On may 392 Valentinian was found hanged at his home at Vienne. Arbogast maintained his innocence and claimed that Valentinian must have committed suicide.
2 CONT Arbogast showed his true dark colors by elevating an imperial official named Eugenius as emperor of the West. Civil war broke out and in 394 Theodosius defeated Eugenius and Arbogast.
