2 CONT
2 CONT Dengizich (spelled Δεγγιζίχ in Priscus' account; died 468 or 469) ruler of the Akatziroi, was a son of Attila the Hun. The word "Dengizich" means little sea in old Turkic (*Däŋiziq, where *-ziq is the diminutive suffix). This is a
2 CONC lso said to be the root of the name Genghis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some time during his reign, the Utigurs (Onogurs) first crossed the river Volga (according to Zacharias Rhetor). Priscus is clearer saying that in 463AD a mixed Saragur, Urog and Unogur embassy asked Byzantium for an alliance havi
2 CONC ng been dislodged by the Avars' drive towards the west
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Dengizyk poległ za sprawą podstępu Chelchala, jego odciętą głowę wystawiono na widok publiczny w Konstantynopolu jako oznakę tryumfu
