1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ernak
2 CONT
2 CONT Ernak was the last known ruler of the Huns, and the third son of Attila.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Attila's favorite son,[3] because as a certain Hun explained to him, the Hunnic prophets prophesied his genos would fail, but would be restored by this son.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ernak has often been identified with Irnik from the Nominalia of the Bulgarian khans, who is noted as a descendant of the Dulo clan and leader of the Bulgars for 150 years, starting approximately from 437 AD.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
