2 CONT Godegisel, King of the Vandals was born circa 359. He was the son of Visimar Asdingi.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Godegisel, King of the Vandals married free woman (?) before 379. 
2 CONT
2 CONT King of the Vandals at Gaul in 406. Godegisel, King of the Vandals invaded Gaul in 406. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died circa 411. At the the time Rome was captured and destroyed by the Goths, "the Vandals were hard-pressed in their war against the Franks, their King Godegisel was killed and about 20,000 of their front-line troops had been 
2 CONC slaughtered, so that, if the army of the Alani had not come to their rescue in time, the entire nation of Vandals would have been wiped out."[2]
2 CONT
