2 CONT ### GAILAMIR [Gelimar] (-533).  Procopius names “Gelimer, Gelaridis filius, Genzonis nepos, pronepos Gizerici”[63].  He succeeded in 530 as GAILAMIR King of the Vandals in Africa, after deposing his cousin Hilderic.  A Byzantine a
2 CONC rmy, led by Belisarius, conquered the Vandal Kingdom of Africa in 533, vanquishing Gailimar at Decimum and Tricamarum[64].  Gregory of Tours records that Gailamir "was broken in battle by the forces of the Roman Empire and ended h
2 CONC is life and his reign at the same moment"[65]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ### TZAZO .  Procopius names “Tzazo…Gelimeris frater” when recording that he landed in Sardinia[66]. 
