1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Theodoric Strabo[1] (died 481) was an Ostrogoth chieftain who was involved in the politics of the Byzantine Empire during the reigns of Byzantine Emperors Leo I, Zeno and Basiliscus. He was a rival for the leadersh
2 CONC ip of the Ostrogoths with his kinsman Theoderic the Great, who would ultimately supplant him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodoric called Strabo, son of Triarius, was a chieftain of the Thracian Goths; he had two brothers. The wife of the Alan general Aspar was his sister.[2] Strabo had a wife, Sigilda, and a son called Recitach. He was a contempora
2 CONC ry of the more famous Theodoric the Amal, who was a Moesian Goth of the royal Amal family, and who would become known as Theoderic the Great.[3] Around 459, he is attested as in friendly relationship with the Byzantine Empire, pos
2 CONC sibly one of the foederati, and receiving an annual subsidy by the Byzantines.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodoric_Strabo
