2 CONT
2 CONT == Thorismund, king of the Visigoths
2 CONT * Reign: 20 June 451 – 453
2 CONT * Predecessor: [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodoric-I-king-of-the-Visigoths/6000000010646052427?through=6000000000499350741 Theodoric I]
2 CONT * Successor: [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodoric-II-king-of-the-Visigoths/6000000033110974854?through=6000000000499350741 Theodoric II]
2 CONT * Died: 453 (aged 33)
2 CONT * Father: [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodoric-I-king-of-the-Visigoths/6000000010646052427?through=6000000000499350741 Theodoric I]
2 CONT * Spouse: (none known)
2 CONT * Religion: Arian Christianity
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thorismund ''(38 languages)''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thorismund''' (also '''Thorismod''' or '''Thorismud''', as manuscripts of our chief source confusingly attest[1]) (c. 420–453), became king of the Visigoths after his father Theodoric was killed in the Battle of the Catalaunian
2 CONC  Plains (also called Battle of Châlons) in 451 CE. He was murdered in 453 and was succeeded by his brother Theodoric II. .. ... ....
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TOULOUSE.htm#dauTheodericMHuneric
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         '''THORISMUND''' (-murdered 453).  Iordanes names (in order) "Friderichum et Eurichum, Retemerim et Himnerith" as four of the sons of "Theoderido", specifying that their father took his two older sons "Thorismud et Theo
2 CONC dericum maiores natu" when he fought at the battle of the Catalaunian Fields, dated to 451[71].  Herimannus names "Torismod filius Theodorus rex Gothorum" when recording that he succeeded his father[72].  He was elected to succeed
2 CONC  his father in 451 as '''THORISMUND King of the Visigoths'''.  Iordanes records that he also fought "in campis statim Catalaunicisis" and succeeded after the death of his father in the same battle[73].  He made war on the Alans at
2 CONC  Orléans and marched again on Arles[74].  The Chronicon of Bishop Idatius records that “Thorismo Rex Gothorum” was killed by “Theuderico et Frederico fratribus” in 453[75].  The Chronica Regum Visigotthorum records that “Thurismod
2 CONC us” reigned for three years[76]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT El resumen proporcionado por Mercedita Florencia Saez Iribarnegaray:
2 CONT
2 CONT Es asesinado por sus hermanos Federico y Teodorico, comprados por los romanos. Había reinado 2 años. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel's summary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationships:
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Theodoric I, King of the Visigoths and (Unknown) daughter of Alaric I
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Unknown daughter (d. after 442), married to (in 429) and repudiated by (in 442) Huneric I, King of the Vandals 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Theoderic II, King of the Visigoths (453-466) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Frideric (Friderico), Visigoth military leader 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Euric I, King of the Visigoths (b. after 435, 466-484) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Retemiris (Ricimer), Visigoth military leader 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Himnerith, Visigoth military leader 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Unknown daughter, m. 449 in Toulouse Richgar/Requiario, King of the Suevi (d. 456)
2 CONT
2 CONT No spouse or children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Basic information and justifications:
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: There is no information on his date or location of birth. However, the Visigoths did invade Iberia (present Spain) starting in 409 (he was probably born after this date), and it would not be unreasonable to presume his birt
2 CONC h took place there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: He was strangled to death by his two brothers, presumably in Toulouse. No specific date given other than in 453. His rule was said, however, to have been three years, which may indicate a death late in the year (the passage
2 CONC  on his duration of rule may have meant that it ended in his third year, or after June 20, 453, the second anniversary of his election). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse, children, burial: No information is given.
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: King of the Visigoths (20 June 451-late 453)
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate names: Thorismund, Turismundo, Torismond
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
