1 NAME Abarwiz ben al Masmughan (Al-Masmughan Malik) /of the house of Karen and founder of the Masmughan Kingdom of Damavand/
2 GIVN Abarwiz ben al Masmughan (Al-Masmughan Malik)
2 _MARNM of the house of Karen and founder of the Masmughan Kingdom of Damavand
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ref:page 39 The History of al-Tabari Vol. 28: 'Abbasid Authority Affirmed: The Early ... By Jane Dammen McAuliffe
2 CONT
2 CONT Masmughan Mardanshah of Damavand  The Masmughans of Damavand (Middle Persian: Masmughan-i Dumbawand, New Persian: مس مغان دماوند, meaning Great Magians of Damavand) were a local dynasty, which ruled Damavand and its surrounding ar
2 CONC eas from ca. 651 to 760. The founder of the dynasty was a Karenid[1] named Mardanshah of Damavand.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Masmughans of Damavand are first mentioned by Al-Tabari, where the Masmughan Mardanshah of Damavand reportedly aided the Mihranid Siyavakhsh at Ray against the Arabs. The forces of Siyavakhsh and Mardanshah, were, however, def
2 CONC eated. Mardanshah then made peace with the Arabs in return for an annual tribute.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 748/749, Abu Muslim sought to subdue the Masmughan but his general Musa ibn Kab was ambushed by the local forces who enjoyed the advantage of the terrain, which forced him to return to Ray. In 758/759 due to disputes between Ab
2 CONC arwiz and his brother, who is simply called Masmughan in Arabic sources, Abarwiz then went over to the Caliph Al-Mansur who gave him a pension. In some Arabic sources Abarwiz is called Al-Masmughan Malik (malik of the Masmughans),
2 CONC  and is known for his bravery.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 760, Masmughan, the brother of Abarwiz, was at war against his father-in-law, the Dabuyid ispahbadh Khurshid, but when he heard about the Abbasid expedition to Tabaristan, he made peace with the latter. The Arabs then defeated 
2 CONC the ispahbadh and the Masmughan, who was captured along with his daughters Bakhtariya and Shakla. One of these daughters became the wife of Al-Mahdi
