1 NAME Maziar /Kayusiyya Bavand/
2 GIVN Maziar
2 _MARNM Kayusiyya Bavand
1 NAME Maziar ibn Qarin
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Iranian_History/Last_Remnants_of_Sassanian_Rule#Deyleman
2 CONT
2 CONT Maziar was the grandson of the Padhuspani prince Shahriar I and a scion of the House of Karen. He was a contemporary of Afshin Kheydar and Babak Khorramdin. Maziar led the revolutionary troops at the height of the Persian national
2 CONC ist struggle even defeating the forces of Caliph once.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the medieval historian Ibn Esfandyar in his Tarikh-e-Tabaristan, Maziar is said to have proclaimed: "Afshin Kheydar, son of Kavus and Babak, and I had made an oath and allegiance that we take the country back from the
2 CONC  Arabs and transfer the government and the country back to the family of Kasraviyan(Sassanid)."
2 CONT
2 CONT Maziar was eventually betrayed by his brother Kuhyar and handed over to the soldiers of the Caliphate. He was deported to Baghdad in 839. While some accounts say that he was executed, other say that he took poison to escape humili
2 CONC ation at the hands of the Arabs.
