1 TITL "Queen of Queens of Persia"
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was one of Papak's daughters, a local ruler in Pars; her brothers were Shapur, Ardashir I, and Balash. She later became the wife of Ardashir I in accordance with the Zoroastrian law of consanguine marriage.[1] 
2 CONC She was thus given the title of bānbishnān bānbishn ("Queen of Queens") and is assumed to have been represented the figure on the far right of the investiture relief of Ardashir at Naqsh-e Rajab. She was most likely also the mothe
2 CONC r of Ardashir's son Shapur I, and later lost her title of bānbishnān bānbishn after the death of her husband in 242..
