1 OCCU Roman Emperor (306-May 22, 337), Empereur de Rome, Roman Emperor, 57th Emporer of Rome, 306-307 Emperor of Roman Empire.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Flavius ​​Hannibalianus (* after 289; † before 337) was a son of the Roman emperor Constantius Chlorus and his second wife Theodora and thus a half-brother of Constantine the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT New !!: Anastasia (daughter Constantius ’I.) and Flavius ​​Hannibalianus · See more»
2 CONT
2 CONT Helena (mother of Constantine the Great)
2 CONT Solidus Helena's Capitoline Museum Flavia Iulia Helena (* 248/250 in Drepanon, today Karamürsel, in Bithynia; † probably on August 18 around 330 in Nicomedia, today İzmit), also Helena of Constantinople, was the mother of the Roma
2 CONC n Emperor Constantine, from to which she was appointed Augusta.
2 CONT
2 CONT New !!: Anastasia (daughter Constantius ’I.) and Helena (mother Constantine the Great) · See more»
2 CONT
2 CONT Julius Constantius
2 CONT Flavius ​​Julius Constantius (* after 289; † 337 in Constantinople) was a son of the Roman emperor Constantius ChlorusZonaras 12, 33.
