2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Seeck, in RE VI 2 (1909) 2085, holds for a date not earlier than 293 and possibly as late as 298. But Barnes, New Empire 34, argues convincingly for 289 or 290. Nevertheless it is to be noted that she remained childless for the 
2 CONC first nine or ten years of her marriage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Jul. Or. 1.5C-D. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 Lact. Mort Pers. 27.1; Aur. Vict. Epit. 40.12; Zosimus 2.10. 6 and 2.39.1. The notion that Constantine and Fausta had been betrothed some years earlier is rightly rejected by Drijvers, "Flavia Maxima Fausta" 501-503. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Pan. Lat. 7 (edd. Baehrens, Mynors, and Nixon and Rodgers) or 6 (ed. Galletier). 
2 CONT
