1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tranquillina
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Furia Sabinia Tranquillina
2 CONT
2 CONT Sabinia Tranquillina Augusta[1]
2 CONT  Museo Chiaramonti, ca. 241
2 CONT
2 CONT Born
2 CONT
2 CONT c. 225
2 CONT
2 CONT Died
2 CONT
2 CONT aft. 244
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse
2 CONT
2 CONT Gordian III
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Furia
2 CONT
2 CONT Furia Sabinia Tranquillina or Sabinia Tranquillina (ca 225 - aft. 244) was the Empress of Rome and wife of Emperor Gordian III. She was the young daughter of the Praetorian Prefect Timesitheus by an unknown wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 241 her father was appointed the head of the Praetorian Guard by the Roman Emperor Gordian III. In May that year, Tranquillina had married Gordian. She became a Roman Empress and received the honorific title of Augusta. Her mar
2 CONC riage to Gordian was an admission by the young emperor of both political indispensability of Timesitheus and Tranquillina’s suitability as an empress.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 243, Tranquillina's father suddenly died and was replaced with Philip the Arab, as head of the Praetorian Guard. When Gordian was killed in February 244, Philip became the new emperor. Tranquillina survived her husband. She had
2 CONC  no sons with him. Christian Settipani suggests that they had a daughter, (Furia) (b. ca 244), most likely posthumous, who married (Marcus Maecius Orfitus) (b. ca 245), son of Marcus Maecius Probus (b. ca 220), married to Pupiena 
2 CONC Sextia Paulina Cethegilla (b. ca 225), paternal grandson of Marcus Pomponius Maecius Probus and maternal grandson of Marcus Pupienus Africanus Maximus (son of his protector Emperor Pupienus Maximus) and wife Cornelia Marullina, by
2 CONC  whom she had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tranquillina
