2 CONT Eutropia, Maximianus Herculius' Wife
2 CONT
2 CONT Eutropia was of Syrian extraction and her marriage to Maximianus Herculius seems to have been her second. She bore him two children: Maxentius and Fausta . An older daughter, Theodora , may have been a product of her first marriag
2 CONC e. Fausta became the wife of Constantine I , while her sister Theodora was the second spouse of his father Constantius I Chlorus . She apparently survived all her children, with the possible exception of her daughter Fausta who se
2 CONC ems to have died in 326, and was alive in 325. She is also said to have become a Christian.
2 CONT
