1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hazrat Khawaja Mu'in al-Din Hasan Chishti (1 February 1143 – 15 March 1236) was a Persian Muslim scholar, preacher, and Sufi saint, known for establishing the Chishti order in the Indian subcontinent. He was the so
2 CONC n of Hazrat Syed Ghiyath al-Din Hasan and Syeda Bibi Umm al-Wara. Born in Sistan, in present-day Iran or Afghanistan, he travelled extensively through Central Asia and the Middle East, studying under various scholars before eventu
2 CONC ally settling in Ajmer, in present-day India.
2 CONT
2 CONT He became known for his emphasis on compassion, charity, and inclusivity, attracting followers from diverse backgrounds. His teachings focused on spiritual devotion, service to humanity, and the spread of Islamic values through pe
2 CONC aceful means. After his death, his shrine in Ajmer became a major centre of pilgrimage, and his influence continued through the Chishti order, which played a significant role in the cultural and spiritual life of South Asia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mu%27in_al-Din_Chishti
2 CONT https://muslimviews.co.za/khwaja-muin-al-din-chishtis-spiritual-legacy-in-south-asia-and-beyond/
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrine_of_Mu%27in_al-Din_Chishti
