1 CONT Flavius Mauricius Tiberius Augustus (b. 539 in Arabissus, Cappadocia, d. 602 in Constantinople), known in English as Maurice and in Greek as Maurikios, was a Byzantine Emperor who ruled from 582-602. He was one of the most importa
1 CONC nt rulers of the early 'Byzantine' era, whose reign was troubled by almost unending wars on all frontiers.
1 CONT
1 CONT Persian War and accession to the throne
1 CONT Maurice originated from Arabissus in Cappadocia and was a successful commander-in-chief. He was adopted by his predecessor Tiberius II, and succeeded him after the latter?s death. His reign is an accurately documented era of the l
1 CONC ate classical antiquity (most important source is the historian Theophylact Simocatta). During a war with the Sassanid Empire, already under way in 572 under Justin II, Maurice was in service as commander-in-chief from 579 on. He 
1 CONC scored a crushing victory against the Persians in 581. A year later, he married Constantina, the Emperor?s daughter. On August 13th, he succeeded his father-in-law. At that time, he ruled a bankrupt Empire, paying extremely high t
1 CONC ribute to the Avars, its Balkan provinces thoroughly devastated by the Slavs and at war with Persia.
1 CONT
