1 CONT !REIGNED: King of Franks (481 - 511) 
1 CONT King of France 
1 CONT Founder of the Empire of the Franks 
1 CONT
1 CONT c.466-511, Frankish king (481-511), founder of the MEROVINGIAN monarchy. He rose from tribal chief to sole leader of the Salian FRANKS by dint of patience and murder. He won Gaul and SW Germany by fighting the Romans, Alemanni, Bu
1 CONC rgundians, and Visigoths. His wife, St. Clotilda, encouraged his conversion (496) to Christianity. 
1 CONT
1 CONT FILE: Concise Columbia Electronic Encyclopedia Copyright 1994, Columbia University Press. 
1 CONT
1 CONT FILE: Peter Grard Gentala 
1 CONT
1 CONT REIGNED: King of Cologne 
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTE: kinsman of Clovis I "the Great", King of the Salic Franks 
1 CONT
