0 @N6000000001355550614@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT From ages 7 to 17 he was a Byzantine prisoner, but returned to his father's kingdom after and became king in 474 at the death of his father. Between 474 and 488, Theodoric and the Eastern Roman Emperor Zeno fought each other. In 4
1 CONC 88 Theodoric, while allied with Zeno, invaded Italy (at the time under the Germanic king Odoacer), which was taken in three battles. Odoacer surrendered in 493, and was slain by Theodoric.While Theodoric was Arian, he tolerated al
1 CONC l sects of Christianity. Theodoric was succeeded on this death in 526 by his daughter Amalasunthaas regent for her son Athalaric. King of the Ostrogoths 474-526
0 @N6000000001354335614@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT From ages 7 to 17 he was a Byzantine prisoner, but returned to his father's kingdom after and became king in 474 at the death of his father. Between 474 and 488, Theodoric and the Eastern Roman Emperor Zeno fought each other. In 4
1 CONC 88 Theodoric, while allied with Zeno, invaded Italy (at the time under the Germanic king Odoacer), which was taken in three battles. Odoacer surrendered in 493, and was slain by Theodoric.While Theodoric was Arian, he tolerated al
1 CONC l sects of Christianity. Theodoric was succeeded on this death in 526 by his daughter Amalasunthaas regent for her son Athalaric. King of the Ostrogoths 474-526
0 @N6000000003949897600@ NOTE He was of the Arian religion.  He was a member of the Amal clan which claimed descent from Gaut, the Scandinavian god of war.  He and his 2 brothers, Valamir and Vidimir, became the firs Amals to step into the light of history, ar
1 CONC ound 450 as leaders of Hunnic Goths.  He ruled the western subkingdom under his brother Valamir and then assumed the kingship after Valamir's death in 469/470.  He went to war against the anti-Gothic neighbors in Sueva.  He broke 
1 CONC the Hunnic power of Attila's sons in the Battle of Nedao in 454.   Ruled 463-474.  See "History of the Goths" Herwig Wolfram, 1987
0 @N6000000002187923612@ NOTE Theodemir
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Theodemir was king of the Ostrogoths of the Amal Dynasty. He ruled jointly with his two brothers, and was a vassal of Attila the Hun. He was married to Erelieva, with whom he had two children: Theodoric (454-526) and Amalafrida. W
1 CONC hen Theodemir died in 474, Theodoric succeeded him as king.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT none King of the Ostrogoths
1 CONT ?-474 Succeeded by:
0 @N6000000001355552247@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT Sister of Theodoric the Great, King of the Ostrogoths, and mother of Theodahad, King of the Ostrogoths. Her second husband was Thrasamund, King of the Vandals.
