0 @N6000000002187923631@ NOTE Amalafrida
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Amalafrida was the daughter of Theodemir, king of the Ostrogoths, and his wife Erelieva. She was the sister of Theodoric the Great, also king of the Ostrogoths, and mother of Theodahad, also king of the Ostrogoths. Her second husb
1 CONC and was Thrasamund, king of the Vandals. She had two children: the aforementioned Theodahad and Amalaberga, who married Hermanfrid, king of the Thuringii. It is not known who the father of these children was.
0 @N6000000003949475970@ NOTE a cc of the book "History of the Goths" by Herwig Wolfram (first published in germany 1979)
1 CONT He has a genealogical chart for the Amali's. It is different from the postings in that it shows Amfleda (she married Thrasamund) is a sister of Theodoric instead of being a daughter. Theodoric's daughters are listed as follows:
1 CONT Thiudigotho married Alaric II and begot Amalaric
1 CONT Ostrogotho married Sigismund (a Burgundian king)
1 CONT Amalasuintha married Eutharic and begot Athalaric
1 CONT also, begot Matasuntha who married 1st Vitigis and then Germanus (cousin of Justinian)
1 CONT With a retinue of 1000 elite troops and 5000 servants, she went to Carthage as an element of Theodoric's policy of a barbarian balance of power.
