0 @N6000000001744804619@ NOTE [s2.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT After overcoming rivalries, escaping a number of attempts on his life, and taking advantage of the deaths of his brothers, Chlotar succeeded in reestablishing the unity of the Regnum Francorum in 558 AD. However, his death in 561 
1 CONC led to further division of the kingdom between his sons, into Paris, Burgundy, Austrasia and Soissons, which led to new rivals and bloody conflict. (Wenzler, The Kings of France, 1995).
1 CONT
1 CONT also see source: Church of JC of the LDS "Ancestral File" CD-Rom database, ver 4.17.After overcoming rivalries, escaping a number of attempts on his life, and taking advantage of the deaths of his brothers, Chlotar succeeded in re
1 CONC establishing the unity of the Regnum Francorum in 558 AD. However, his death in 561 led to further division of the kingdom between his sons, into Paris, Burgundy, Austrasia and Soissons, which led to new rivals and bloody conflict
1 CONC . (Wenzler, The Kings of France, 1995).
1 CONT
1 CONT also see source: Church of JC of the LDS "Ancestral File" CD-Rom database, ver 4.17.
