1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT King of the Salian Franks 426-447
1 CONT Semi-legendary King of the Salian Franks and father of Merovech, founder of the Merovingian Dynasty. Called ", the Long Hair" or ", the Hairy" because of the length of his hair. From then on the Merovingians were called the "Long 
1 CONC Haired Kings" and the cutting of a king's hair represented his loss of royal power.
1 CONT According to legend his father was Pharamond (r.409-426), the first King of the Salian Franks after the departure of the Romans from Gaul. In history, Clodio was probably real. He lived in Thuringian territory, and ruled at the sa
1 CONC me time as the semi-legendary kings Theudemer and Richemer. All that is known of his reign is that he took the town of Cambrai from the Romans. He was succeeded by his semi-legendary sonMerovech. (Unlike Merovech and Clodio, Child
1 CONC eric I, Merovech's son, was very real and cannot be considered fictional.)
1 CONT [Fix.FTW]
