0 @N6000000002187705320@ NOTE Baderic
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Baderic or Boderic was born in ca. 480 and died in ca. 529 and was co-king of the Thuringians. He and his brothers Hermanfrid and Berthar succeeded their father Bisinus to the rule over the Thuringians. After Hermanfrid defeated B
1 CONC erthar in battle, he invited King Theuderic I of Metz to help him defeat Baderic in return for half of the kingdom. Theuderic I agreed and Baderic was defeated and killed in 529. Hermanfrid however kept the kingdom.
0 @N6000000003051129291@ NOTE [Wikipedia, "Baderic", retrieved 4 Oct 07]
1 CONT Baderic, Baderich, or Boderic (c.480-c.529), son of Bisinus and Basina, was a co-king of the Thuringii. He and his brothers Hermanfrid and Berthar succeeded their father Bisinus. After Hermanfrid defeated Berthar in battle, he inv
1 CONC ited King Theuderic I of Metz to help him defeat Baderic in return for half of the kingdom. Theuderic I agreed and Baderic was defeated and killed in 529. Hermanfrid became the sole king.
0 @N6000000000437396329@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Half King Name Suffix:<NSFX> Of Thuringia
0 @N6000000002244390198@ NOTE He greatly expanded the area under Frankish hemony. He was a proven soldier
1 CONT before he came to the throne and claimed control of the peoples from the
1 CONT Baltic to beyond the Danube. By minting coins bearing his, rather than the
1 CONT Byzantine emperor's, effigy and name, Theodebert asserted his independence of
1 CONT Constantinople, against which he apparently even invisioned mounting an
1 CONT expedition. He was the most appealing of the Merovingians and , Clovis apart,
1 CONT perhaps the most remarkable personality among them (succeeded by Theobald).
0 @N6000000001353750113@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT King of Austrasia 534-548
1 CONT Theudebert I was the son of Theuderic I, King of Metz, and grandson of Clovis I. During the reign of his father, Theudebert defeated and killed the Danish king Chlochilaich who had invaded Metz. He then helped his father and uncle
1 CONC , King Chlothar I of Soissons, defeated King Hermanfrid of the Thuringians. Theudebert then was engaged to Wisigard, daughter of King Wacho of the Longobards, but did not marry her. He instead married Guntheuc while campaigning in
1 CONC  Spain. When Theuderic I died, Chlothar, Childebert, and Theudebert all fought for the throne, but Theudebert won it as King of Austrasia (almost as large as Metz). Theudebert then married Deuteria, with whom he had a son Theudeba
1 CONC ld. His uncles pushed him to finally marry Wisigard, but she soon died and Theudebert married again (not Deuteria). He died mysteriously ill in 548, and was succeeded by his son Theudebald as King of Austrasia.
1 CONT [Fix.FTW]
