0 @N6000000002176649502@ NOTE Ephemeral successor to his father, Theodoric II, as king of Austrasia and
1 CONT Burgundy; he reigned only a mater of weeks before the hostility of the
1 CONT Austrasian nobility, led by Arnuk of Metz and Pepin I, to his
1 CONT great-grandmother Brunhild led to his overthrow and the reunification of the
1 CONT Frankish lands under Chlotar II. Both Sigebert II and Brunhild were killed by
1 CONT Chlotar.
0 @N6000000002188311874@ NOTE Sigebert II
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Sigebert II (601-613) was king of Burgundy and Austrasia (613). Bastard son of Theuderic II, he succeeded his father in 613; but the mayor of the palace of Austrasia, Warnachar, feared that at his young age he would fall under the
1 CONC  influence of his great-grandmother Brunhilda. Brunhilda had brought him before a national assembly, where he was proclaimed by the nobles, who did homage to him over both his father's kingdoms. But Warnachar and Rado, mayor of th
1 CONC e palace of Burgundy, abandoned the cause of Brunhilda and the young king and joined with Clotaire II of Neustria, promising not to rise in defence of the queen-regent and recognising Clotaire as rightful regent and guardian of Si
1 CONC gebert. Brunhilda and Sigebert met Clotaire's army on the Aisne, but the Patrician Aletheus, Duke Rocco, and Duke Sigvald deserted the host and the grand old woman and her king had to flee. They got as far as the Orbe before Clota
1 CONC ire's minions caught up with them by lake Neuchâtel. Both of them and Sigebert's younger brother Corbo were executed by Clotaire's orders. Brunhilda was tortured on the rack for three days before being ripped apart between four ho
1 CONC rses, thus ending the long and bloody feud between Austrasia and Neustria, and reuniting the two kingdoms. Clotaire then ruled the entire realm of the Franks.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT This article does not cite any references or sources. (January 2008)
1 CONT Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unverifiable material may be challenged and removed.
1 CONT Sigebert II
1 CONT Merovingian Dynasty
1 CONT Born: 601 Died: 613
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Theuderic II King of Austrasia and Burgundy
1 CONT 613 Succeeded by
1 CONT Clotaire II
