0 @N6000000002187968256@ NOTE Gunthamund
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Gunthamund (c.450-496), King of the Vandals and Alans (484-496) was the third king of the north African Kingdom of the Vandals. He succeeded his unpopular uncle Huneric, and for that reason alone, enjoyed a rather successful reign
1 CONC .
1 CONT
1 CONT Gunthamund was the second son born to Gento, the fourth and youngest son of Geiseric, the founder of the Vandal kingdom in Africa. Because most of Geiseric's immediate family died young, Gunthamund found himself as the eldest male
1 CONC  member of the family when Huneric died in 484. In accordance with his grandfather's laws on the succession, he was proclaimed king.
1 CONT
1 CONT Gunthamund benefitted throughout his reign from the fact that the Vandals' most powerful rivals, the Visigoths, Ostrogoths and the Byzantine Empire, were all heavily involved in wars. Although the Vandals' power had fallen off gre
1 CONC atly since its zenith under Geiseric, they enjoyed peace under Gunthamund. Gunthamund also eased up on the persecutions of the Catholics that had begun under Huneric, a move which eased some of the unrest in his kingdom, and stabi
1 CONC lized the kingdom's economy, which was on the verge of collapse under Huneric.
1 CONT
1 CONT Unfortunately for the Vandals, Gunthamund followed in the footsteps of his immediate family and died rather young, in his mid-forties. He was succeeded by his brother Thrasamund, who was not as effective in ruling the kingdom.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Huneric King of the Vandals
1 CONT 484–496 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Thrasamund
