0 @N6000000002187580471@ NOTE Gratian the Elder
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Gratian the Elder was the father of the Roman emperors, Valentinian I and Valens and the grandfather of Gratian.
1 CONT
1 CONT Gratian began his career as a staff officer, but later became tribune, and then Comes Africae. He was sent to Britannia in the 340s and given the title Comes Britanniarum, in command of a field army (comitatus). The crisis that pr
1 CONC ecipitated this is not known however. After his retirements, Emperor Constantius II confiscated all of Gratian properties, because of a suspected support of Magnentius.
0 @N6000000001355550911@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT Emperor of Rome in the East 364-378
1 CONT Valens was chosen by his brother Valentinian I to rule in the East when he ascended to the throne in 364. In 367, Valens warred with the Visigoths, and finally in 376 he allowed the Visigoths to live in the Empire. They breached t
1 CONC his good faith and attacked the Romans at Adrianople in 378. Valens was killed in the battle.
