0 @N6000000002187923939@ NOTE Theodoric II
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Theodoric II (in Spanish Teodorico) murdered his older brother Thorismund to become king of the Visigoths in 453 CE. Edward Gibbon writes that "he justified this atrocious deed by the design which his predecessor had formed of vio
1 CONC lating his alliance with the empire." During Theodoric's reign the Kingdom of the Visigoths, centered in what is now Aquitaine, continued to be a federate of the western Roman Empire. In 462 the empire ceded Septimania to Theodori
1 CONC c.
1 CONT
1 CONT Upon his death in 466 Theodoric's younger brother Euric succeeded him to the throne.
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT External link
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Edward Gibbon, History of the Decline and Fall of the Roman Empire, chapter 36
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT  This biography of a European noble is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it.
1 CONT
1 CONT
